WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.006 --> 00:00:08.966
<i>Citizens of Oz.</i>

2
00:00:10.051 --> 00:00:12.219
<i>there's been 12 tide turns</i>

3
00:00:12.303 --> 00:00:16.265
<i>since the Wicked Witch of the West
escaped with our Grimmerie.</i>

4
00:00:16.349 --> 00:00:18.184
<i>Shield your children.</i>

5
00:00:18.267 --> 00:00:20.602
<i>Trust no animals.</i>

6
00:00:20.686 --> 00:00:24.481
<i>She will be eliminated.</i>

7
00:00:24.565 --> 00:00:27.109
<i>Until then. the Wizard's vision</i>

8
00:00:27.193 --> 00:00:30.821
<i>for the Oz of tomorrow marches on.</i>

9
00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:35.576
Do it. Move!

10
00:00:38.037 --> 00:00:40.539
-Load it up.
-Come on. Let's go! Move!

11
00:00:41.707 --> 00:00:42.874
No speaking.

12
00:00:43.376 --> 00:00:45.252
The Wizard needs the road finished.

13
00:00:51.968 --> 00:00:53.219
Move it! Move it!

14
00:00:53.302 --> 00:00:54.553
Come on. let's move!

15
00:00:56.472 --> 00:00:57.973
Fill up that basket!

16
00:01:03.604 --> 00:01:05.439
Keep moving.

17
00:01:05.523 --> 00:01:06.524
Come on.

18
00:01:09.569 --> 00:01:10.945
Come on. Keep moving.

19
00:01:12.697 --> 00:01:13.531
Get up!

20
00:01:18.619 --> 00:01:19.661
Come on!

21
00:01:31.716 --> 00:01:32.925
Settle down!

22
00:01:39.265 --> 00:01:40.474
Whoa. whoa. whoa. whoa.

23
00:01:45.688 --> 00:01:46.605
Get back!

24
00:01:53.112 --> 00:01:54.947
Retreat! Guards. retreat!

25
00:01:56.407 --> 00:01:57.408
It's the Witch!

26
00:03:02.556 --> 00:03:04.224
The Witch! She's back!

27
00:03:10.731 --> 00:03:13.608
♪ <i>Every day. more Wicked</i> ♪

28
00:03:13.693 --> 00:03:16.737
♪ <i>Every day. the terror grows</i> ♪

29
00:03:16.821 --> 00:03:21.075
♪ <i>All of Oz is ever on alert</i> ♪

30
00:03:21.158 --> 00:03:24.244
♪ <i>That's the way with Wicked</i> ♪

31
00:03:24.328 --> 00:03:27.205
♪ <i>Spreading fear where'er she goes</i> ♪

32
00:03:27.289 --> 00:03:31.459
♪ <i>Seeking out new victims she can hurt</i> ♪

33
00:03:31.544 --> 00:03:33.712
♪ <i>Like some terrible green blizzard</i> ♪

34
00:03:33.796 --> 00:03:36.048
♪ <i>Throughout the land. she flies</i> ♪

35
00:03:36.132 --> 00:03:40.632
♪ <i>Defaming our poor Wizard
With her calumnies and lies</i> ♪

36
00:03:42.346 --> 00:03:46.846
♪ <i>She lies</i> ♪

37
00:03:48.853 --> 00:03:53.353
♪ <i>She lies</i> ♪

38
00:03:55.234 --> 00:03:56.235
Go. go!

39
00:03:56.318 --> 00:03:57.444
Release them!

40
00:04:08.372 --> 00:04:12.793
♪ <i>Save us from the Wicked</i> ♪

41
00:04:12.877 --> 00:04:17.089
♪ <i>Shield us so we won't be hexed!</i> ♪

42
00:04:17.173 --> 00:04:20.384
♪ <i>Give us warning
Where will she strike next?</i> ♪

43
00:04:21.469 --> 00:04:23.721
♪ <i>Where will she strike next?</i> ♪

44
00:04:24.680 --> 00:04:29.180
♪ <i>Where will she strike next?</i> ♪

45
00:04:34.356 --> 00:04:37.650
♪ <i>When I stop the Wizard</i> ♪

46
00:04:37.735 --> 00:04:40.404
♪ <i>All Oz will applaud</i> ♪

47
00:04:40.488 --> 00:04:43.532
♪ <i>How I saved them from the Wizard</i> ♪

48
00:04:43.616 --> 00:04:46.160
♪ <i>By revealing he's a fraud</i> ♪

49
00:04:47.411 --> 00:04:50.580
♪ <i>If I can just make them
Believe in the truth</i> ♪

50
00:04:50.664 --> 00:04:53.375
♪ <i>That all that he says is a lie</i> ♪

51
00:04:53.918 --> 00:04:58.418
♪ <i>That's when they'll finally bid
The Wizard goodbye</i> ♪

52
00:05:08.057 --> 00:05:09.933
<i>-Come with me.</i>
<i>-What?</i>

53
00:05:10.017 --> 00:05:11.309
<i>To meet the Wizard.</i>

54
00:05:11.393 --> 00:05:13.937
<i>The Wizard will see you now.</i>

55
00:05:14.688 --> 00:05:16.731
♪ <i>Dearest Glinda. you are still the best</i> ♪

56
00:05:16.816 --> 00:05:17.817
Well. I guess.

57
00:05:17.900 --> 00:05:20.277
♪ <i>Others are Good
But you're the Goodliest</i> ♪

58
00:05:20.361 --> 00:05:23.530
♪ <i>We feel merry. we feel cheery
Just to gaze on your reflection</i> ♪

59
00:05:23.614 --> 00:05:28.114
♪ <i>Only you disprove the theory
That you can't improve perfection</i> ♪

60
00:05:31.664 --> 00:05:33.040
Thank you.

61
00:05:33.123 --> 00:05:35.625
Good. Good. Good. Good. Good.

62
00:05:36.210 --> 00:05:38.462
Good.

63
00:05:43.676 --> 00:05:45.803
She's so good.

64
00:05:47.012 --> 00:05:49.597
<i>Glinda the Good.</i>

65
00:05:50.140 --> 00:05:54.640
♪ <i>La. la. la. la</i> ♪

66
00:05:55.187 --> 00:05:59.687
♪ <i>La. la. la. la</i> ♪

67
00:06:00.359 --> 00:06:04.859
♪ <i>La. la. la. la</i> ♪

68
00:06:05.781 --> 00:06:10.281
♪ <i>La. la. la. la. la. la. la
La. la. la. la. la. la. la. la. la</i> ♪

69
00:06:11.161 --> 00:06:15.661
♪ <i>La. la. la. la. la. la. la
La. la. la. la. la. la. la. la. la</i> ♪

70
00:06:29.513 --> 00:06:33.433
♪ <i>Save us from the Wicked</i> ♪

71
00:06:33.517 --> 00:06:37.896
♪ <i>Every night our voices wail</i> ♪

72
00:06:37.980 --> 00:06:42.480
♪ <i>Save us from this fear and victimhood</i> ♪

73
00:06:43.569 --> 00:06:47.030
♪ <i>We believe in Glinda</i> ♪

74
00:06:47.114 --> 00:06:50.617
♪ <i>With her magic. she'll prevail</i> ♪

75
00:06:50.701 --> 00:06:55.201
♪ <i>She will make it end the way it should</i> ♪

76
00:06:58.250 --> 00:07:02.750
♪ <i>When at last the Wicked is defeated</i> ♪

77
00:07:03.797 --> 00:07:08.297
♪ <i>By the Good</i> ♪

78
00:07:09.511 --> 00:07:13.389
♪ <i>The Good</i> ♪

79
00:07:13.474 --> 00:07:16.477
♪ <i>Wicked is defeated.</i> ♪

80
00:07:16.560 --> 00:07:21.060
♪ <i>By the Good</i> ♪

81
00:07:27.404 --> 00:07:29.697
There's a quoncert in Quox.
if you wanna attend. next week.

82
00:07:29.782 --> 00:07:31.074
Oh. perhaps.

83
00:07:31.158 --> 00:07:33.702
The Quadling Quorum wants to honor you.
They're just not sure for what yet.

84
00:07:33.786 --> 00:07:34.620
Good to hear.

85
00:07:34.703 --> 00:07:37.330
And someone sent pastries.

86
00:07:37.414 --> 00:07:39.791
-Good for us.
-Send these to my hovel. please.

87
00:07:39.875 --> 00:07:41.918
The gowns from last week?

88
00:07:42.002 --> 00:07:43.753
Oh. maybe. uh.
give to the under-fortunate.

89
00:07:43.837 --> 00:07:46.047
-Oh. of course.
-Good idea.

90
00:07:46.131 --> 00:07:47.257
You know. while we're at it.

91
00:07:47.341 --> 00:07:49.801
we really should look into
trademarking the word "good."

92
00:07:49.885 --> 00:07:51.595
-Ooh!
-Oh!

93
00:07:51.679 --> 00:07:55.349
That's go-- I mean. I'm goosified.
My follicles are screaming.

94
00:07:55.432 --> 00:07:56.975
I love my job so much.

95
00:07:57.059 --> 00:07:58.018
Oh. good

96
00:07:58.102 --> 00:08:00.354
Madame Morrible.

97
00:08:00.437 --> 00:08:03.189
Forgive me for keeping you waiting.
I had no idea.

98
00:08:04.274 --> 00:08:06.651
Has something happened? Is it Elphaba?

99
00:08:06.735 --> 00:08:08.319
You mean the Wicked Witch.

100
00:08:08.862 --> 00:08:09.904
Right. of course.

101
00:08:09.989 --> 00:08:11.782
Come in. come in.

102
00:08:11.865 --> 00:08:12.699
Mrs. Morrible. I can--

103
00:08:12.783 --> 00:08:14.034
Would you like us to take minutes for you?

104
00:08:14.118 --> 00:08:16.620
I can get you. like. a little snack.
You want a little snack?

105
00:08:16.704 --> 00:08:18.497
Like a cherry frazzle or a juice puff?

106
00:08:19.832 --> 00:08:22.417
"Mrs. Morrible"? She's not married.

107
00:08:22.501 --> 00:08:24.211
You shut...

108
00:08:24.837 --> 00:08:27.548
With the Yellow Brick Road grand opening ahead

109
00:08:27.631 --> 00:08:30.383
and the Wicked Witch attacks
growing bolder.

110
00:08:30.467 --> 00:08:32.427
the public is on edge.

111
00:08:32.511 --> 00:08:37.011
So it's more important than ever
that you lift everyone's spirits.

112
00:08:38.183 --> 00:08:39.767
as only you can.

113
00:08:41.895 --> 00:08:42.896
Accordingly.

114
00:08:45.274 --> 00:08:46.817
Oh. Madame. I love it.

115
00:08:47.443 --> 00:08:48.444
What is it?

116
00:08:49.611 --> 00:08:51.696
Your new mode of transport.

117
00:08:51.780 --> 00:08:55.408
Your very own vehicular spherical globule.

118
00:08:55.951 --> 00:08:57.994
So. like. a bubble?

119
00:09:01.331 --> 00:09:02.332
Sure.

120
00:09:10.090 --> 00:09:11.549
Was that supposed to happen?

121
00:09:11.633 --> 00:09:12.634
It's all right.

122
00:09:13.510 --> 00:09:14.761
Are you sure?

123
00:09:20.559 --> 00:09:21.935
Does that do what I think it does?

124
00:09:25.022 --> 00:09:26.231
No!

125
00:09:31.862 --> 00:09:33.154
I can't.

126
00:09:34.406 --> 00:09:35.907
No way!

127
00:09:39.745 --> 00:09:41.288
I'm obsessulated.

128
00:09:41.371 --> 00:09:44.165
The Wizard had it crafted
especially for you.

129
00:09:44.249 --> 00:09:48.211
His Ozness feels it vital that you.
as our Good Witch.

130
00:09:48.295 --> 00:09:50.046
also be airborne.

131
00:09:50.589 --> 00:09:52.299
I agree.

132
00:09:54.134 --> 00:09:58.054
But don't fret over your inability
to produce any actual magic.

133
00:09:58.138 --> 00:10:01.516
This invention will
disguise your deficiency.

134
00:10:01.600 --> 00:10:05.228
The Bubble's mechanism
is cleverly concealed.

135
00:10:05.312 --> 00:10:08.857
People will assume
that you are causing it to float

136
00:10:08.941 --> 00:10:11.526
through your own witchly powers.

137
00:10:11.610 --> 00:10:14.029
So. just let them assume.

138
00:10:15.280 --> 00:10:16.114
Right.

139
00:10:16.198 --> 00:10:18.241
But don't forget this.

140
00:10:30.129 --> 00:10:32.965
The wand really sells it.

141
00:10:37.386 --> 00:10:39.346
I'll see you at the opening ceremony.

142
00:10:39.429 --> 00:10:41.139
Thank you so much.

143
00:10:57.781 --> 00:10:59.574
<i>A magic wand?</i>

144
00:10:59.658 --> 00:11:01.826
Happy birthday. Galinda!

145
00:11:04.788 --> 00:11:07.207
It's what I've wanted most of all.

146
00:11:07.291 --> 00:11:08.875
Come on. give it a go.

147
00:11:08.959 --> 00:11:11.711
Yeah. try it out!

148
00:11:11.795 --> 00:11:16.174
-Magic! Magic! Magic! Magic!
-Come on!

149
00:11:30.314 --> 00:11:31.648
Oh.

150
00:11:31.732 --> 00:11:33.191
I forgot to say the spell.

151
00:11:33.275 --> 00:11:35.986
-Oh. yeah. Come on. Yeah. Yeah.
-Makes sense.

152
00:11:37.196 --> 00:11:41.696
I hereby commandify
that something magical shall happen!

153
00:11:43.744 --> 00:11:45.537
She can't even make a spark.

154
00:11:45.621 --> 00:11:46.455
Look.

155
00:11:47.331 --> 00:11:48.457
There's a rainbow.

156
00:11:48.999 --> 00:11:50.000
What is that?

157
00:11:52.336 --> 00:11:53.211
Did you make that?

158
00:11:54.046 --> 00:11:55.464
Um...

159
00:11:55.547 --> 00:11:57.840
Well. you know how I love rainbows.

160
00:11:58.467 --> 00:12:00.177
-Oh. wow.
-Do it again!

161
00:12:00.260 --> 00:12:01.511
That's my friend!

162
00:12:02.095 --> 00:12:03.346
I knew she could do it.

163
00:12:03.889 --> 00:12:06.600
-Go see the rainbow!
-Isn't it fantastic?

164
00:12:06.683 --> 00:12:07.809
I knew she had magic.

165
00:12:07.893 --> 00:12:10.520
Who is ready for some cake?

166
00:12:17.277 --> 00:12:19.153
What's wrong. dearest?

167
00:12:19.821 --> 00:12:21.280
You got everything you wanted.

168
00:12:21.365 --> 00:12:25.865
I know. but I wanna be magical.
For real. And...

169
00:12:27.287 --> 00:12:28.788
I'm not.

170
00:12:28.872 --> 00:12:30.748
Oh. but. darlingest.

171
00:12:31.458 --> 00:12:33.668
everyone loves you.

172
00:12:34.211 --> 00:12:35.462
Believe me.

173
00:12:36.171 --> 00:12:37.964
that's all you'll ever need.

174
00:12:39.466 --> 00:12:40.925
Where's that smile?

175
00:12:41.426 --> 00:12:42.718
That's my girl.

176
00:12:57.985 --> 00:13:00.612
Sweetheart. you coming?

177
00:13:04.283 --> 00:13:05.284
Come on!

178
00:13:32.436 --> 00:13:33.520
Glinda!

179
00:13:39.776 --> 00:13:41.068
Fellow Ozians.

180
00:13:41.570 --> 00:13:43.238
Good news.

181
00:13:43.322 --> 00:13:46.199
Now. at last.
all roads lead to the Wizard.

182
00:13:47.159 --> 00:13:49.870
♪ <i>Oh. what a celebration
We'll have today</i> ♪

183
00:13:49.953 --> 00:13:51.412
♪ <i>Thank Goodness</i> ♪

184
00:13:51.496 --> 00:13:54.624
♪ <i>Let's have a celebration
The Glinda way</i> ♪

185
00:13:54.708 --> 00:13:56.167
♪ <i>Thank Goodness</i> ♪

186
00:13:56.251 --> 00:13:59.879
♪ <i>Finally. a day that's totally
Wicked Witch-free</i> ♪

187
00:13:59.963 --> 00:14:02.590
♪ <i>We couldn't be happier</i> ♪

188
00:14:02.674 --> 00:14:03.716
♪ <i>Thank Goodness</i> ♪

189
00:14:05.135 --> 00:14:07.345
Thank Goodness for you. Glinda.

190
00:14:07.429 --> 00:14:10.515
and your handsome swain. Prince Fiyero.

191
00:14:10.599 --> 00:14:14.144
newly appointed captain of the Gale Force.

192
00:14:14.227 --> 00:14:18.727
assembled by the Wizard himself
to capture the Wicked Witch.

193
00:14:19.107 --> 00:14:22.860
Tell us. Captain. How does it feel?

194
00:14:22.944 --> 00:14:23.986
It's frustrating.

195
00:14:24.780 --> 00:14:28.575
But I became captain to find her.
and I will keep on searching until I do.

196
00:14:28.658 --> 00:14:30.409
No!

197
00:14:31.745 --> 00:14:33.121
Being engaged.

198
00:14:38.001 --> 00:14:39.127
We're engaged?

199
00:14:39.211 --> 00:14:40.503
Surprised?

200
00:14:41.171 --> 00:14:42.005
Yes.

201
00:14:42.089 --> 00:14:44.382
Good. We hoped you'd be.

202
00:14:44.466 --> 00:14:45.675
The Wizard and I.

203
00:14:45.759 --> 00:14:47.677
Aw.

204
00:14:48.720 --> 00:14:53.220
♪ <i>We couldn't be happier
Right. dear?</i> ♪

205
00:14:53.517 --> 00:14:57.062
♪ <i>Couldn't be happier
Right here</i> ♪

206
00:14:57.145 --> 00:15:00.148
♪ <i>Look what we've got
A fairy-tale plot</i> ♪

207
00:15:00.232 --> 00:15:04.110
-♪ <i>Our very own happy ending</i> ♪
-Aw.

208
00:15:04.194 --> 00:15:08.615
♪ <i>Where we couldn't be happier
True. dear?</i> ♪

209
00:15:08.698 --> 00:15:11.033
♪ <i>Couldn't be happier.</i> ♪

210
00:15:11.118 --> 00:15:15.618
♪ <i>And we're happy to share
Our ending vicariously</i> ♪

211
00:15:15.831 --> 00:15:17.999
♪ <i>With all of you</i> ♪

212
00:15:18.083 --> 00:15:20.168
♪ <i>He couldn't look handsomer</i> ♪

213
00:15:20.252 --> 00:15:22.587
♪ <i>I couldn't feel humbler.</i> ♪

214
00:15:22.671 --> 00:15:25.674
♪ <i>We couldn't be happier</i> ♪

215
00:15:25.757 --> 00:15:29.469
♪ <i>Because happy is what happens</i> ♪

216
00:15:29.553 --> 00:15:34.053
♪ <i>When all your dreams come true</i> ♪

217
00:15:37.436 --> 00:15:40.981
And. Glinda. dear. we are happy for you.

218
00:15:41.064 --> 00:15:42.523
As Press Secretary.

219
00:15:42.607 --> 00:15:47.107
I've striven to ensure that all of Oz
knows the story of your braverism

220
00:15:48.238 --> 00:15:52.075
in the face of the terrifying
Wicked Witch of the West.

221
00:15:53.785 --> 00:15:57.205
♪ <i>I hear she has an extra eye
That always remains awake</i> ♪

222
00:15:58.123 --> 00:16:02.460
♪ <i>I hear that she can shed her skin
As easily as a snake</i> ♪

223
00:16:02.544 --> 00:16:06.965
♪ <i>I hear some rebel animals
Are giving her food and shelter</i> ♪

224
00:16:07.048 --> 00:16:11.548
♪ <i>I hear her soul is so unclean
Pure water can melt her</i> ♪

225
00:16:13.638 --> 00:16:15.306
♪ <i>Melt her!</i> ♪

226
00:16:15.390 --> 00:16:19.519
♪ <i>Please. somebody go and melt her!</i> ♪

227
00:16:19.603 --> 00:16:22.022
People are so empty-headed.
they'll believe anything.

228
00:16:22.856 --> 00:16:25.942
If you'll excuse us just a clock tick.

229
00:16:26.026 --> 00:16:27.277
Come with me. dearest.

230
00:16:29.362 --> 00:16:30.946
What is going on?

231
00:16:31.615 --> 00:16:32.866
People are watching.

232
00:16:32.949 --> 00:16:35.284
I can't just stand there grinning.
pretending to go along with all this.

233
00:16:35.368 --> 00:16:39.038
Do you think I like hearing them say
those awful things about her? I hate it.

234
00:16:39.122 --> 00:16:42.375
Then what are we doing here? Let's go.
Let's go. Let's just get out of here.

235
00:16:42.459 --> 00:16:43.668
I can't.

236
00:16:43.752 --> 00:16:46.921
I can't when there are people
looking to me to raise their spirits.

237
00:16:48.006 --> 00:16:49.424
You can't leave...

238
00:16:50.425 --> 00:16:52.593
because you can't resist this.

239
00:16:53.136 --> 00:16:54.554
That's the truth.

240
00:16:56.765 --> 00:16:58.391
Well. maybe I can't.

241
00:17:01.186 --> 00:17:02.187
Is that so wrong?

242
00:17:02.938 --> 00:17:04.189
I mean. who could?

243
00:17:04.272 --> 00:17:05.273
Well. you know who could.

244
00:17:06.107 --> 00:17:08.651
We both know who could and who has.

245
00:17:08.735 --> 00:17:11.571
And I have to find her. because
if someone else gets there first. she--

246
00:17:11.655 --> 00:17:13.490
Fiyero. I'm worried for her too.

247
00:17:13.573 --> 00:17:14.907
And miss her.

248
00:17:16.493 --> 00:17:18.828
Can't you see
she doesn't want to be found?

249
00:17:20.121 --> 00:17:22.123
You've got to face it.

250
00:17:22.832 --> 00:17:24.542
She's made her choice.

251
00:17:33.969 --> 00:17:34.886
You're right.

252
00:17:41.851 --> 00:17:42.935
And look...

253
00:17:44.938 --> 00:17:47.315
if it makes you happy.
of course I'll marry you.

254
00:17:51.361 --> 00:17:53.529
It'll make you happy too. right?

255
00:17:54.656 --> 00:17:56.282
You know me. I'm always happy.

256
00:18:00.328 --> 00:18:02.621
Fiyero.

257
00:18:10.422 --> 00:18:11.881
Thanks plenty. dearest.

258
00:18:14.134 --> 00:18:15.260
He's. um..

259
00:18:15.802 --> 00:18:18.721
-He's gone to fetch me a refreshment.
-Aw!

260
00:18:19.264 --> 00:18:20.765
He's so thoughtful that way.

261
00:18:28.023 --> 00:18:32.523
♪ <i>That's why I couldn't be happier</i> ♪

262
00:18:34.696 --> 00:18:38.950
♪ <i>No. I couldn't be happier</i> ♪

263
00:18:39.034 --> 00:18:41.911
♪ <i>Though it is. I admit</i> ♪

264
00:18:41.995 --> 00:18:44.122
♪ <i>The tiniest bit</i> ♪

265
00:18:44.205 --> 00:18:48.705
♪ <i>Unlike I anticipated</i> ♪

266
00:18:49.336 --> 00:18:53.423
♪ <i>But I couldn't be happier</i> ♪

267
00:18:53.506 --> 00:18:57.635
♪ <i>Simply couldn't be happier</i> ♪

268
00:18:57.719 --> 00:19:00.263
♪ <i>Well. not "simply"</i> ♪

269
00:19:00.347 --> 00:19:04.809
♪ <i>'Cause getting your dreams
It's strange. but it seems</i> ♪

270
00:19:04.893 --> 00:19:09.393
♪ <i>A little. well. complicated</i> ♪

271
00:19:10.148 --> 00:19:14.648
♪ <i>There's a kind of a sort of cost</i> ♪

272
00:19:15.695 --> 00:19:20.195
♪ <i>There's a couple of things get lost</i> ♪

273
00:19:21.951 --> 00:19:26.451
♪ <i>There are bridges you cross
You didn't know you crossed</i> ♪

274
00:19:26.873 --> 00:19:31.373
♪ <i>Until you've crossed</i> ♪

275
00:19:32.796 --> 00:19:36.883
♪ <i>And if that joy. that thrill</i> ♪

276
00:19:38.551 --> 00:19:43.051
♪ <i>Doesn't thrill like you think it will</i> ♪

277
00:19:44.557 --> 00:19:45.683
♪ <i>Still</i> ♪

278
00:19:46.518 --> 00:19:49.020
♪ <i>With this perfect finale</i> ♪

279
00:19:49.104 --> 00:19:52.398
♪ <i>The cheers and the ballyhoo</i> ♪

280
00:19:52.482 --> 00:19:56.360
♪ <i>Who wouldn't be happier?</i> ♪

281
00:19:57.028 --> 00:20:00.656
♪ <i>So I couldn't be happier</i> ♪

282
00:20:01.491 --> 00:20:05.953
♪ <i>Because happy is what happens</i> ♪

283
00:20:06.037 --> 00:20:10.537
♪ <i>When all your dreams come true</i> ♪

284
00:20:12.752 --> 00:20:15.379
♪ <i>Well. isn't it?</i> ♪

285
00:20:16.840 --> 00:20:19.300
♪ <i>Happy is what happens</i> ♪

286
00:20:19.384 --> 00:20:23.884
♪ <i>When your dreams come true</i> ♪

287
00:20:24.723 --> 00:20:27.308
♪ <i>We love you. Glinda
If we may be so frank</i> ♪

288
00:20:27.392 --> 00:20:28.768
♪ <i>Thank Goodness</i> ♪

289
00:20:28.852 --> 00:20:31.437
♪ <i>For all this joy
We know who we've got to thank</i> ♪

290
00:20:31.521 --> 00:20:33.189
♪ <i>Thank Goodness</i> ♪

291
00:20:33.273 --> 00:20:34.691
♪ <i>That means the Wizard. Glinda</i> ♪

292
00:20:34.774 --> 00:20:36.150
♪ <i>And fiancé</i> ♪

293
00:20:36.234 --> 00:20:39.237
♪ <i>They couldn't be Goodlier</i> ♪

294
00:20:39.320 --> 00:20:41.196
♪ <i>She couldn't be lovelier</i> ♪

295
00:20:41.281 --> 00:20:43.574
♪ <i>We couldn't be luckier</i> ♪

296
00:20:43.658 --> 00:20:45.951
♪ <i>I couldn't be happier</i> ♪

297
00:20:46.035 --> 00:20:49.997
♪ <i>Thank Goodness</i> ♪

298
00:20:50.081 --> 00:20:54.581
♪ <i>Today</i> ♪

299
00:20:54.961 --> 00:20:56.545
♪ <i>Thank Goodness for today</i> ♪

300
00:20:57.380 --> 00:21:01.880
♪ <i>Thank Goodness for today</i> ♪

301
00:21:10.810 --> 00:21:12.978
It's the Wicked Witch! Take cover!

302
00:21:14.481 --> 00:21:15.982
Mount up!

303
00:21:20.278 --> 00:21:22.989
Glinda! Take cover. everyone!

304
00:21:24.991 --> 00:21:27.451
Everyone. please.
Don't be alarmed.

305
00:21:29.454 --> 00:21:31.038
She won't hurt you. It's okay.

306
00:21:31.122 --> 00:21:32.790
She wants to kill us all!

307
00:21:33.625 --> 00:21:34.626
Look!

308
00:21:50.767 --> 00:21:51.809
Gale Force. go!

309
00:21:57.148 --> 00:21:58.440
-Fiyero!
-Hyah!

310
00:21:58.525 --> 00:22:00.485
Come on. Hyah!

311
00:22:01.027 --> 00:22:01.986
No. come.

312
00:22:02.570 --> 00:22:03.571
Move!

313
00:22:40.567 --> 00:22:41.651
Halt!

314
00:23:13.683 --> 00:23:15.768
Captain. do you see anything?

315
00:23:23.818 --> 00:23:24.860
No.

316
00:23:25.570 --> 00:23:26.737
Come on.

317
00:23:26.821 --> 00:23:29.406
We must not rest
until we capture that Wicked Witch.

318
00:23:46.633 --> 00:23:48.343
Come on! Let's go!

319
00:23:48.426 --> 00:23:50.761
-Let's move out.
-Fall in.

320
00:24:16.204 --> 00:24:17.371
Fiyero.

321
00:24:19.123 --> 00:24:20.207
Even you.

322
00:24:58.788 --> 00:24:59.914
Madame Governor?

323
00:25:00.707 --> 00:25:04.085
That proposed new regulation.
the Animal Anti-Motility law.

324
00:25:04.168 --> 00:25:05.169
What law?

325
00:25:06.546 --> 00:25:09.549
Animals would need a permit to travel.

326
00:25:09.632 --> 00:25:12.885
Munchkinland is the one place
in Oz it hasn't been ratified.

327
00:25:12.969 --> 00:25:15.096
The League of Governors
is urging you to sign.

328
00:25:15.179 --> 00:25:17.347
Nessa. you're not going to sign that.

329
00:25:17.432 --> 00:25:18.766
But if I don't...

330
00:25:20.393 --> 00:25:23.187
people will say.
"She's just like her sister."

331
00:25:28.651 --> 00:25:30.861
Give us a clock tick. Avaric.

332
00:25:39.829 --> 00:25:40.913
Boq...

333
00:25:40.997 --> 00:25:45.497
Forgive me. It's just that
Elphaba abandoned me when I needed her.

334
00:25:45.668 --> 00:25:47.878
She didn't even come see me
when Father died.

335
00:25:47.962 --> 00:25:49.964
Only you did that.

336
00:25:51.257 --> 00:25:55.757
Oz only knows how I'd have coped with
all of this without you.

337
00:26:10.109 --> 00:26:12.486
And I'm glad I could be there for you.

338
00:26:15.323 --> 00:26:19.201
But I've been thinking for a while now...

339
00:26:19.285 --> 00:26:20.286
Yes?

340
00:26:21.829 --> 00:26:23.956
I think it's time I moved on.

341
00:26:29.420 --> 00:26:30.421
I see.

342
00:26:33.925 --> 00:26:36.469
Well. if that's how you feel.

343
00:26:38.137 --> 00:26:39.972
think it's best you leave.

344
00:26:41.349 --> 00:26:42.350
Now.

345
00:26:52.944 --> 00:26:53.945
Nessa.

346
00:26:54.445 --> 00:26:57.114
this won't be the last time
we'll see each other.

347
00:26:58.199 --> 00:26:59.366
Oh. I know.

348
00:27:08.543 --> 00:27:10.294
<i>Attention. passengers.</i>

349
00:27:10.378 --> 00:27:14.006
<i>This is the final boarding
for the Emerald City Unlimited.</i>

350
00:27:14.090 --> 00:27:16.342
<i>Doors will be closing shortly.</i>

351
00:27:16.425 --> 00:27:19.636
<i>Please step inside and make way
for boarding passengers.</i>

352
00:27:29.522 --> 00:27:31.398
<i>Visiting someone special?</i>

353
00:27:31.482 --> 00:27:32.983
<i>Get a new Ozfit.</i>

354
00:27:33.067 --> 00:27:36.111
<i>Visit the Wizard's Emporium
in downtown Emerald City.</i>

355
00:27:36.195 --> 00:27:37.196
Next.

356
00:27:37.280 --> 00:27:39.782
<i>Limited time discount
for travelers arriving today.</i>

357
00:27:39.866 --> 00:27:42.201
-Excuse me. um. my train is boarding in--
-Travel permit?

358
00:27:44.036 --> 00:27:45.037
What?

359
00:27:45.121 --> 00:27:47.414
All Munchkins are forbidden
to leave Munchkinland

360
00:27:47.498 --> 00:27:50.417
without express written permission
of the governor.

361
00:27:53.588 --> 00:27:56.507
She insisted it go
into effect immediately.

362
00:27:57.717 --> 00:28:00.219
<i>...reminder to all passengers...</i>

363
00:28:00.303 --> 00:28:01.887
Stop pushing me.

364
00:28:01.971 --> 00:28:03.722
-Go!
-No. Mommy. Mommy.

365
00:28:03.806 --> 00:28:06.475
-Keep your hands off my family.
-I don't wanna hear it. Munchkins.

366
00:28:07.018 --> 00:28:09.395
-Move! Forward now. Munchkins.
-Go.

367
00:28:09.478 --> 00:28:12.397
This is outrageous.
You cannot treat us like this.

368
00:28:12.940 --> 00:28:14.232
Move along. Munchkins.

369
00:28:14.317 --> 00:28:15.318
Next.

370
00:28:15.401 --> 00:28:17.319
This is not the Oz I know.

371
00:28:17.403 --> 00:28:18.987
-This is un-Ozian!
-Back in line.

372
00:28:19.071 --> 00:28:20.530
Step back. What did I say?

373
00:28:20.615 --> 00:28:22.908
Step... Munchkins. step back.

374
00:28:40.885 --> 00:28:42.303
Watch your footing.

375
00:28:43.262 --> 00:28:44.846
Next group. Come on. children.

376
00:28:45.514 --> 00:28:47.974
-Let's move. We have to leave.
-All right. stay together!

377
00:28:49.560 --> 00:28:52.187
Come along now. Keep moving.

378
00:28:53.272 --> 00:28:55.065
Eyes on your children. please.

379
00:28:59.612 --> 00:29:01.780
Don't worry. I'm with you.
I'll never leave you.

380
00:29:01.864 --> 00:29:03.073
Don't go too fast.

381
00:29:04.116 --> 00:29:05.242
What is all this?

382
00:29:05.326 --> 00:29:07.202
-Watch your step.
-What are you doing?

383
00:29:07.286 --> 00:29:09.162
Come. children. Quickly.

384
00:29:09.247 --> 00:29:10.414
We must get out of Oz.

385
00:29:10.498 --> 00:29:12.374
Don't do this. Please.

386
00:29:12.458 --> 00:29:14.334
-Keep moving.
-Don't leave Oz.

387
00:29:14.418 --> 00:29:17.045
Join with me. Help me fight the Wizard.

388
00:29:17.129 --> 00:29:20.257
And wait for the monkeys to carry us off?

389
00:29:20.341 --> 00:29:22.676
That's what happens
to animals who speak out.

390
00:29:22.760 --> 00:29:24.011
And they're never seen again.

391
00:29:24.095 --> 00:29:25.096
No.

392
00:29:25.930 --> 00:29:27.932
Oz wouldn't be Oz without all of you.

393
00:29:28.474 --> 00:29:30.434
And I know you're frightened
but this is home.

394
00:29:31.143 --> 00:29:32.435
Belongs to all of us.

395
00:29:32.520 --> 00:29:34.563
Elphaba.

396
00:29:39.151 --> 00:29:40.068
Dulcibear.

397
00:29:40.152 --> 00:29:41.611
Oh. little one.

398
00:29:44.740 --> 00:29:46.450
I've missed your bear hugs.

399
00:29:47.785 --> 00:29:50.078
We can't stay here.

400
00:29:50.162 --> 00:29:51.955
It's become rotten.

401
00:29:52.498 --> 00:29:54.958
There's only one thing left
for us to do...

402
00:29:55.626 --> 00:30:00.126
escape through that tunnel
to The Place Beyond Oz.

403
00:30:02.758 --> 00:30:05.469
They say The Place Beyond Oz is just...

404
00:30:07.888 --> 00:30:08.972
...emptiness.

405
00:30:13.853 --> 00:30:14.979
How will you survive?

406
00:30:15.062 --> 00:30:17.189
How will you survive here?

407
00:30:17.982 --> 00:30:21.944
No one in Oz will be happy
until you're dead.

408
00:30:32.663 --> 00:30:34.831
Why would you want to stay?

409
00:30:39.211 --> 00:30:40.503
I don't know.

410
00:30:42.923 --> 00:30:45.133
♪ <i>Why do I love this place</i>

411
00:30:46.469 --> 00:30:49.263
♪ <i>That's never loved me?</i> ♪

412
00:30:52.433 --> 00:30:56.311
♪ <i>A place that seems to be devolving</i> ♪

413
00:30:57.938 --> 00:31:00.231
♪ <i>And even wanting to</i> ♪

414
00:31:01.817 --> 00:31:06.317
♪ <i>But Oz is more than just a place</i> ♪

415
00:31:07.615 --> 00:31:11.660
♪ <i>It's a promise. an idea</i> ♪

416
00:31:12.995 --> 00:31:17.495
♪ <i>And I want to help make it come true</i> ♪

417
00:31:19.251 --> 00:31:23.751
♪ <i>Why should a land have so much meaning</i> ♪

418
00:31:24.507 --> 00:31:27.718
♪ <i>When dark times befall it?</i> ♪

419
00:31:27.802 --> 00:31:30.262
♪ <i>It's only land</i> ♪

420
00:31:30.346 --> 00:31:34.846
♪ <i>Made of dirt and rock and loam</i> ♪

421
00:31:36.018 --> 00:31:40.518
♪ <i>It's just a place that's familiar</i> ♪

422
00:31:43.734 --> 00:31:48.234
♪ <i>And home's just what we call it</i> ♪

423
00:31:50.491 --> 00:31:54.991
♪ <i>But there's no place like home</i> ♪

424
00:31:56.997 --> 00:31:58.623
♪ <i>Don't we all know</i> ♪

425
00:32:00.334 --> 00:32:04.834
♪ <i>There's no place like home</i> ♪

426
00:32:06.465 --> 00:32:09.009
Try to understand.

427
00:32:09.093 --> 00:32:11.512
We just can't fight anymore.

428
00:32:12.054 --> 00:32:14.306
We have to.

429
00:32:16.225 --> 00:32:18.602
♪ <i>When you feel you can't fight anymore</i> ♪

430
00:32:18.686 --> 00:32:21.689
♪ <i>Just tell yourself</i> ♪

431
00:32:21.772 --> 00:32:25.692
♪ <i>There's no place like home</i> ♪

432
00:32:26.485 --> 00:32:29.070
♪ <i>When you feel
It's not worth fighting for</i> ♪

433
00:32:29.155 --> 00:32:31.323
♪ <i>Compel yourself</i> ♪

434
00:32:31.407 --> 00:32:35.907
♪ <i>Because there's no place like home</i> ♪

435
00:32:36.912 --> 00:32:38.747
♪ <i>When you want to leave</i> ♪

436
00:32:38.831 --> 00:32:41.875
♪ <i>Discouraged and resigned</i> ♪

437
00:32:41.959 --> 00:32:46.459
♪ <i>That's what they want you to do</i> ♪

438
00:32:47.089 --> 00:32:51.589
♪ <i>But think how you will grieve
For all you leave behind</i> ♪

439
00:32:52.428 --> 00:32:56.928
♪ <i>Oz belongs to you too</i> ♪

440
00:32:59.560 --> 00:33:02.145
♪ <i>Those who would take it from you</i> ♪

441
00:33:02.229 --> 00:33:05.232
♪ <i>Spout a lie to sell yourself</i> ♪

442
00:33:05.316 --> 00:33:09.153
♪ <i>You go their way or go</i> ♪

443
00:33:09.236 --> 00:33:12.113
♪ <i>It's them we'll be defeating</i> ♪

444
00:33:12.198 --> 00:33:14.825
♪ <i>If we keep on repeating</i> ♪

445
00:33:14.909 --> 00:33:19.409
♪ <i>There's no place like home</i> ♪

446
00:33:19.705 --> 00:33:24.205
♪ <i>There's no place like home</i> ♪

447
00:33:26.253 --> 00:33:30.753
♪ <i>There's no place like home</i> ♪

448
00:33:37.139 --> 00:33:41.639
♪ <i>If we just keep fighting for it</i> ♪

449
00:33:42.186 --> 00:33:46.686
♪ <i>We will win back and restore it</i> ♪

450
00:33:48.943 --> 00:33:53.443
♪ <i>There's no place</i> ♪

451
00:33:54.615 --> 00:33:57.117
♪ <i>Like--</i> ♪

452
00:33:57.201 --> 00:33:59.203
Don't listen to her!

453
00:33:59.286 --> 00:34:01.830
Where did he go?

454
00:34:03.415 --> 00:34:07.915
At night. when I close my eyes.
I still see that green face.

455
00:34:10.005 --> 00:34:12.257
I can't believe it.

456
00:34:12.341 --> 00:34:14.384
-Is that you?
-Stay back!

457
00:34:14.468 --> 00:34:16.303
When I was just a cub.

458
00:34:16.387 --> 00:34:19.348
she snatched me
from the only home I ever knew.

459
00:34:19.431 --> 00:34:20.557
You were in a cage.

460
00:34:21.100 --> 00:34:23.519
If I'd have left you there.
you would never have learned to speak.

461
00:34:23.602 --> 00:34:26.396
They say she's the one
who gave the monkeys wings

462
00:34:26.480 --> 00:34:28.315
and gave the Wizard his spies.

463
00:34:28.399 --> 00:34:29.358
Is this true?

464
00:34:34.863 --> 00:34:36.447
It's true.

465
00:34:36.532 --> 00:34:38.200
I cast that spell.

466
00:34:40.869 --> 00:34:42.036
And I have to live with that.

467
00:34:43.956 --> 00:34:45.582
If I'd have known I was being tricked.

468
00:34:45.666 --> 00:34:47.584
if I'd have known why.
I would never have--

469
00:34:48.252 --> 00:34:50.003
The Wizard lies. I can prove it.

470
00:34:50.087 --> 00:34:51.671
And if we stand together...

471
00:34:51.755 --> 00:34:52.714
Dulcibear!

472
00:34:52.798 --> 00:34:54.007
Little one.

473
00:34:54.508 --> 00:34:56.218
I know you'll keep fighting.

474
00:34:57.469 --> 00:34:58.887
because I know you.

475
00:35:11.817 --> 00:35:13.235
Thank you. Boq.

476
00:35:29.501 --> 00:35:32.295
Perhaps a friendly game of cards
once I'm done working?

477
00:35:33.130 --> 00:35:35.173
Whatever you say. Madame Governor.

478
00:35:35.716 --> 00:35:37.467
I asked you to call me Nessa.

479
00:35:38.135 --> 00:35:39.344
Remember?

480
00:35:40.512 --> 00:35:41.513
Boq.

481
00:35:44.892 --> 00:35:47.185
Never mind.
I'll call you when I've finished.

482
00:36:18.926 --> 00:36:21.345
Now. who could have left that door open?

483
00:36:28.769 --> 00:36:29.770
I did.

484
00:36:38.821 --> 00:36:40.447
It's so good to see you.

485
00:36:40.531 --> 00:36:42.032
Why are you here?

486
00:36:44.576 --> 00:36:46.744
I've tried to keep you
out of all of this. but...

487
00:36:48.497 --> 00:36:49.498
I need you.

488
00:36:49.581 --> 00:36:51.708
Thought you might have come to apologize.

489
00:36:52.418 --> 00:36:53.544
Apologize?

490
00:36:53.627 --> 00:36:57.464
Our father died of shame.
and you didn't even bother to show up.

491
00:36:58.006 --> 00:36:59.841
You might at least pretend to be sorry.

492
00:36:59.925 --> 00:37:01.801
For what? He hated me.

493
00:37:01.885 --> 00:37:03.511
That's a wicked thing to say.

494
00:37:03.595 --> 00:37:04.596
No. it's not.

495
00:37:05.180 --> 00:37:06.306
It's just the truth.

496
00:37:07.224 --> 00:37:09.768
-Do you know why?
-What does it matter now?

497
00:37:11.395 --> 00:37:14.106
You're right. Doesn't matter.

498
00:37:16.859 --> 00:37:18.443
Because it's just us.

499
00:37:18.527 --> 00:37:20.695
You're the governor. People will
listen to you. and together. we--

500
00:37:20.779 --> 00:37:22.322
Why should I help you?

501
00:37:22.406 --> 00:37:26.906
You fly around Oz with that book.
helping animals you've never even met.

502
00:37:27.202 --> 00:37:29.829
and not once have you ever thought
to use your powers to help me.

503
00:37:29.913 --> 00:37:32.540
-You never wanted my help.
-I do now!

504
00:37:40.966 --> 00:37:44.135
I want to go back
to the way we were at school.

505
00:37:45.012 --> 00:37:48.306
That night when Boq told me
I was beautiful.

506
00:37:50.893 --> 00:37:53.854
It was the first time
I ever wore these shoes.

507
00:37:55.272 --> 00:37:57.023
There was music.

508
00:38:01.320 --> 00:38:03.488
And everything was still possible.

509
00:38:06.617 --> 00:38:09.536
♪ <i>That night at the Ozdust</i> ♪

510
00:38:10.579 --> 00:38:13.123
♪ <i>Boq danced with me there</i> ♪

511
00:38:14.500 --> 00:38:19.000
♪ <i>And it felt like he loved me then</i> ♪

512
00:38:20.339 --> 00:38:24.839
♪ <i>That night when I felt
I was floating on air</i> ♪

513
00:38:27.054 --> 00:38:31.554
♪ <i>I want to feel that again</i> ♪

514
00:38:32.684 --> 00:38:34.477
Make me feel that again!

515
00:38:34.561 --> 00:38:36.437
Nessa. I wish there was
something I could do. but--

516
00:38:51.411 --> 00:38:52.412
What are you doing?

517
00:38:56.625 --> 00:38:58.001
Oh.

518
00:38:58.085 --> 00:38:59.377
My shoes!

519
00:38:59.962 --> 00:39:02.130
They feel like they're on fire!

520
00:39:19.189 --> 00:39:21.316
I'm floating on air.

521
00:39:24.152 --> 00:39:26.154
Nessa. At last.

522
00:39:27.406 --> 00:39:31.618
♪ <i>I'd always been unsure I could</i> ♪

523
00:39:31.702 --> 00:39:36.202
♪ <i>But finally. from these powers
Something good</i> ♪

524
00:39:38.417 --> 00:39:42.087
♪ <i>Finally. something good</i> ♪

525
00:39:42.170 --> 00:39:44.422
Thank you. Elphaba.

526
00:39:44.506 --> 00:39:45.340
Nessa?

527
00:39:45.424 --> 00:39:47.426
He called me Nessa! It's working!

528
00:39:47.509 --> 00:39:49.302
Nessa. there's something I have to--

529
00:39:50.512 --> 00:39:51.721
Look.

530
00:39:54.766 --> 00:39:55.975
-You.
-Boq.

531
00:39:56.059 --> 00:39:57.143
Stay back!

532
00:39:57.853 --> 00:40:00.730
-It's just me. I'm not gonna hurt you.
-Boq. don't be afraid.

533
00:40:00.814 --> 00:40:03.483
Elphaba just came to lift my spirits.

534
00:40:05.527 --> 00:40:07.862
You did this to make her happy?

535
00:40:07.946 --> 00:40:10.698
I know now anything is possible.

536
00:40:10.782 --> 00:40:12.533
For both of us.

537
00:40:15.078 --> 00:40:16.162
-♪ <i>Nessa?</i> ♪
-Yes?

538
00:40:16.246 --> 00:40:17.789
♪ <i>Uh. Nessa</i> ♪

539
00:40:17.873 --> 00:40:20.959
♪ <i>Surely. now. I'll matter less to you</i> ♪

540
00:40:21.543 --> 00:40:25.296
♪ <i>And you won't mind
My leaving here tonight</i> ♪

541
00:40:25.380 --> 00:40:26.381
Leaving?

542
00:40:27.799 --> 00:40:29.967
♪ <i>The moment when I read</i> ♪

543
00:40:30.719 --> 00:40:32.929
♪ <i>Glinda's going to be wed</i> ♪

544
00:40:33.013 --> 00:40:35.140
♪ <i>To Fiyero</i> ♪

545
00:40:35.223 --> 00:40:36.224
Glinda?

546
00:40:36.725 --> 00:40:38.226
♪ <i>Yes. Nessa. that's right</i> ♪

547
00:40:39.102 --> 00:40:42.146
♪ <i>And I've got to go appeal to her</i> ♪

548
00:40:42.648 --> 00:40:47.148
♪ <i>Express the way I feel to her</i> ♪

549
00:40:51.657 --> 00:40:52.491
Nessa.

550
00:40:55.035 --> 00:40:58.580
I lost my heart to Glinda
the moment I first saw her.

551
00:40:59.122 --> 00:41:00.790
Lost your heart?

552
00:41:03.085 --> 00:41:04.544
Well. we'll see about that.

553
00:41:04.628 --> 00:41:06.671
-Let him go!
-Don't come any closer!

554
00:41:07.798 --> 00:41:10.926
You and your sister.
She's as wicked as you are.

555
00:41:11.009 --> 00:41:13.511
Keeping me here like a prisoner.

556
00:41:13.595 --> 00:41:16.389
-What are you talking about?
-I am talking about my life!

557
00:41:18.725 --> 00:41:20.643
The little that's left of it.

558
00:41:23.647 --> 00:41:26.024
You're gonna lose your heart
to me. I tell you!

559
00:41:26.650 --> 00:41:28.610
If I have to...

560
00:41:29.194 --> 00:41:30.528
I have to...

561
00:41:34.533 --> 00:41:35.700
magic spell you.

562
00:41:35.784 --> 00:41:38.745
There must be a magic spell in here
to capture your heart.

563
00:41:38.829 --> 00:41:41.498
-Nessa. no. That's dangerous.
-What is she doing?

564
00:41:43.250 --> 00:41:44.209
Stop. Nessa!

565
00:41:46.044 --> 00:41:47.879
You're pronouncing the words all wrong!

566
00:41:47.963 --> 00:41:49.089
W-What is she saying?

567
00:41:51.383 --> 00:41:52.509
I'm going.

568
00:41:57.305 --> 00:41:59.223
Ah.

569
00:41:59.307 --> 00:42:00.182
Boq. what is it?

570
00:42:01.101 --> 00:42:02.477
Ah. my heart.

571
00:42:04.771 --> 00:42:07.023
It feels like it's-- like it's shrinking.

572
00:42:07.107 --> 00:42:08.441
-Do something!
-I can't!

573
00:42:08.525 --> 00:42:10.485
A spell from the Grimmerie
can never be reversed.

574
00:42:10.569 --> 00:42:11.570
Boq!

575
00:42:11.653 --> 00:42:13.488
This is all your fault!
If you hadn't come here--

576
00:42:13.572 --> 00:42:15.949
I have to find another spell.
It's the only thing that might work.

577
00:42:16.033 --> 00:42:18.452
Go. now! Go!

578
00:42:27.085 --> 00:42:29.587
♪ <i>Save him. please
Just save him</i> ♪

579
00:42:29.671 --> 00:42:33.174
♪ <i>My poor Boq
My sweet. my brave him</i> ♪

580
00:42:33.258 --> 00:42:37.758
♪ <i>Don't leave me till
My sorry life has ceased</i> ♪

581
00:42:38.263 --> 00:42:40.265
♪ <i>Alone and loveless here</i> ♪

582
00:42:41.141 --> 00:42:44.144
♪ <i>With just the girl in the mirror</i> ♪

583
00:42:44.227 --> 00:42:46.312
♪ <i>Just her and me</i> ♪

584
00:42:46.396 --> 00:42:50.896
♪ <i>The Wicked Witch of the East</i> ♪

585
00:42:54.362 --> 00:42:58.862
♪ <i>We deserve each other</i> ♪

586
00:43:19.387 --> 00:43:20.429
He's sleeping now.

587
00:43:24.476 --> 00:43:25.560
What about his heart?

588
00:43:26.103 --> 00:43:27.104
It's all right.

589
00:43:28.522 --> 00:43:30.065
He won't need one now.

590
00:43:31.566 --> 00:43:32.608
The wedding...

591
00:43:34.611 --> 00:43:35.737
Wait. where are you going?

592
00:43:37.322 --> 00:43:39.907
All the most influential people in Oz
will be there.

593
00:43:39.991 --> 00:43:43.077
It's the perfect opportunity to show them
all the truth about the Wizard.

594
00:43:43.161 --> 00:43:45.329
Oh. please. Stop lying to yourself.

595
00:43:46.164 --> 00:43:49.167
You're going there to find Fiyero.
but it's too late.

596
00:43:49.251 --> 00:43:51.878
Nessa. I have done
everything I could for you.

597
00:43:51.962 --> 00:43:53.588
and it hasn't been enough.

598
00:43:54.422 --> 00:43:55.673
Nothing ever will be.

599
00:44:00.137 --> 00:44:01.471
Elphaba. don't leave me!

600
00:44:04.015 --> 00:44:05.224
Goodbye. Nessa.

601
00:44:06.476 --> 00:44:07.810
I'm off to see the Wizard.

602
00:44:21.741 --> 00:44:23.033
Where am I?

603
00:44:23.118 --> 00:44:24.452
What happened?

604
00:44:25.662 --> 00:44:27.622
It's all right. dearest.
You just--

605
00:44:47.434 --> 00:44:48.435
What have you done?

606
00:44:53.857 --> 00:44:56.401
It wasn't me. I tried to stop her.

607
00:45:06.912 --> 00:45:07.913
Boq. please.

608
00:45:09.748 --> 00:45:11.207
What have you done to me?

609
00:45:11.750 --> 00:45:12.709
You witch!

610
00:45:12.792 --> 00:45:16.003
It wasn't me. it was her! It was Elphaba!

611
00:45:29.768 --> 00:45:30.852
Boq!

612
00:45:33.396 --> 00:45:35.940
<i>Ozians of the Emerald City.</i>

613
00:45:36.024 --> 00:45:40.524
<i>today. the winds shift
and destiny unfolds before our very eyes.</i>

614
00:45:42.405 --> 00:45:43.322
Mm-hmm.

615
00:45:43.406 --> 00:45:47.076
<i>For on this night.
by the glorification of our Wizard.</i>

616
00:45:47.160 --> 00:45:51.660
<i>Glinda the Good and Prince Fiyero Tigelaar
join hands in unification.</i>

617
00:45:52.374 --> 00:45:55.627
Do I have everything I need?
No. I need an earring. please.

618
00:45:55.710 --> 00:45:56.794
Thank you.

619
00:45:58.129 --> 00:46:00.172
Something oldish? Yes.

620
00:46:00.257 --> 00:46:02.550
<i>This is more than just a wedding.</i>

621
00:46:02.634 --> 00:46:04.802
<i>It is a coronation of hope itself.</i>

622
00:46:08.139 --> 00:46:09.431
<i>Something new...</i>

623
00:46:10.350 --> 00:46:12.352
Absolutely.

624
00:46:12.435 --> 00:46:14.645
<i>So let the very foundations of Oz</i>

625
00:46:14.729 --> 00:46:17.481
<i>shimmer with celebratorium</i>

626
00:46:17.565 --> 00:46:20.359
<i>for today. Oz writes a new chapter.</i>

627
00:46:21.278 --> 00:46:25.778
<i>Rejoicify. and Oz shall shine for evermore.</i>

628
00:46:31.246 --> 00:46:32.664
Something bartered...

629
00:46:34.165 --> 00:46:36.375
And something askew.
I need something askew.

630
00:46:42.966 --> 00:46:44.384
Just give me a clock tick.

631
00:46:56.021 --> 00:46:58.106
Elphaba Thropp. I know you're out here.

632
00:46:59.065 --> 00:47:01.525
Just come in before the monkeys spot you.

633
00:47:12.329 --> 00:47:13.330
Elphaba.

634
00:47:14.122 --> 00:47:15.206
Galinda.

635
00:47:18.793 --> 00:47:20.127
Get in. Go.

636
00:47:34.309 --> 00:47:37.228
Elphie. Thank Oz you're alive.

637
00:47:37.854 --> 00:47:39.689
Careful. Your dress.

638
00:47:57.499 --> 00:47:59.834
I still can't believe you get around
on that old thing.

639
00:47:59.918 --> 00:48:01.920
Well. we can't all come and go by bubble.

640
00:48:02.587 --> 00:48:03.421
True.

641
00:48:08.968 --> 00:48:10.010
Are you all right?

642
00:48:10.595 --> 00:48:11.596
I'm fine.

643
00:48:14.307 --> 00:48:15.933
I just wanted to come and see you.

644
00:48:16.017 --> 00:48:17.727
That means a lot to me. Elphie.

645
00:48:18.478 --> 00:48:21.230
-But if anyone discoverates you--
-I know.

646
00:48:21.815 --> 00:48:23.191
I know.

647
00:48:25.985 --> 00:48:28.153
You never saw me. I was never here.

648
00:48:28.238 --> 00:48:30.907
-Do you understand?
-No. I can't bear this anymore.

649
00:48:30.990 --> 00:48:33.909
-I'm taking you to see the Wizard.
-Absolutely not.

650
00:48:33.993 --> 00:48:35.536
-Yes.
-No!

651
00:48:36.871 --> 00:48:39.623
This is between the Wizard and I.

652
00:48:39.707 --> 00:48:42.167
I understand.
But you have to trust me.

653
00:48:42.252 --> 00:48:43.503
I know how to talk to him. and maybe

654
00:48:43.586 --> 00:48:45.379
I could help work something out.

655
00:49:11.948 --> 00:49:13.532
♪ <i>Since I've...</i> ♪

656
00:49:14.284 --> 00:49:15.410
What?

657
00:49:44.564 --> 00:49:45.690
You're done.

658
00:49:48.568 --> 00:49:49.569
It's over.

659
00:49:52.238 --> 00:49:54.281
I had a hunch you'd be coming back to me.

660
00:49:54.365 --> 00:49:56.909
I'm not here for you. I'm here for Oz.

661
00:49:56.993 --> 00:50:01.205
Elphaba. You know. you could've
just exited normally. Just use the door.

662
00:50:02.207 --> 00:50:03.541
Hello?

663
00:50:03.625 --> 00:50:04.959
Yes?

664
00:50:05.460 --> 00:50:06.627
Don't hate me.

665
00:50:06.711 --> 00:50:09.547
It's my wedding day. and you cannot
refuse a wedding wish.

666
00:50:09.631 --> 00:50:11.007
Well. you can. but it's rude.

667
00:50:11.090 --> 00:50:12.091
I don't have time for this.

668
00:50:12.175 --> 00:50:14.260
Now. listen. You and I are gonna
go down there together.

669
00:50:14.344 --> 00:50:17.430
and you are gonna admit to her guests
that you have no real power.

670
00:50:17.514 --> 00:50:19.432
and that you cannot read the Grimmerie.

671
00:50:22.185 --> 00:50:23.728
Why is that funny?

672
00:50:23.811 --> 00:50:26.271
Elphaba. ah. I've missed you.

673
00:50:27.232 --> 00:50:29.776
Can't we start again?

674
00:50:29.859 --> 00:50:30.901
Yes. Please.

675
00:50:31.486 --> 00:50:32.695
-Just say yes.
-No.

676
00:50:32.779 --> 00:50:34.614
Don't you think I wish I could?

677
00:50:34.697 --> 00:50:36.824
I would give anything to go back
to a time when I...

678
00:50:39.911 --> 00:50:43.456
When I actually believed
that you were wonderful.

679
00:50:44.415 --> 00:50:46.458
"The Wonderful Wizard of Oz."

680
00:50:47.460 --> 00:50:49.587
No one believed in you more than I did.

681
00:50:51.965 --> 00:50:53.508
But there's no going back.

682
00:50:54.342 --> 00:50:56.927
And we can't move forward.
not until everyone knows what I know.

683
00:50:57.011 --> 00:50:59.638
-And once they know the truth--
-They're not gonna believe it.

684
00:51:00.974 --> 00:51:03.601
-How can you say that?
-Well. I'm just being straight with you.

685
00:51:03.685 --> 00:51:06.187
I could tell 'em
that I'd been lying to 'em

686
00:51:06.271 --> 00:51:09.357
till I'm. forgive me. blue in the face.

687
00:51:09.440 --> 00:51:11.608
but wouldn't make any difference.

688
00:51:12.819 --> 00:51:14.862
They're never gonna stop believing in me.

689
00:51:14.946 --> 00:51:16.447
You know why?

690
00:51:17.448 --> 00:51:18.740
Because they don't want to.

691
00:51:20.952 --> 00:51:23.371
♪ <i>Take it from a wise. old carny.</i> ♪

692
00:51:24.163 --> 00:51:27.374
♪ <i>Once folks buy into your blarney!</i> ♪

693
00:51:28.209 --> 00:51:32.087
♪ <i>It becomes the thing
They'll most hold on to</i> ♪

694
00:51:36.843 --> 00:51:39.470
♪ <i>Once they've swallowed sham and hokum</i> ♪

695
00:51:40.388 --> 00:51:43.516
♪ <i>Facts and logic won't unchoke em</i> ♪

696
00:51:44.392 --> 00:51:48.354
♪ <i>They'll go on believing
What they want to</i> ♪

697
00:51:51.107 --> 00:51:54.360
♪ <i>Show them exactly what's the score</i> ♪

698
00:51:56.904 --> 00:52:01.404
♪ <i>They'll just believe it even more</i> ♪

699
00:52:11.085 --> 00:52:13.128
♪ <i>Wonderful</i> ♪

700
00:52:14.756 --> 00:52:18.092
♪ <i>They called me "Wonderful"</i> ♪

701
00:52:19.344 --> 00:52:23.844
♪ <i>So I said. "Wonderful?
If you insist"</i> ♪

702
00:52:28.519 --> 00:52:30.062
♪ <i>Wonderful</i> ♪

703
00:52:30.146 --> 00:52:32.815
♪ <i>I will be "Wonderful"</i> ♪

704
00:52:33.441 --> 00:52:36.694
♪ <i>Believe me. it's hard to resist</i> ♪

705
00:52:36.778 --> 00:52:40.364
♪ <i>'Cause it feels wonderful</i> ♪

706
00:52:40.448 --> 00:52:42.867
♪ <i>They think he's wonderful</i> ♪

707
00:52:42.950 --> 00:52:45.202
♪ <i>Hey. look who's wonderful</i> ♪

708
00:52:45.286 --> 00:52:46.996
♪ <i>This corn-fed hick</i> ♪

709
00:52:47.789 --> 00:52:52.289
♪ <i>Who said. "It might be keen
To build a town of green</i> ♪

710
00:52:52.627 --> 00:52:55.921
♪ <i>And a wonderful road of yellow brick"</i> ♪

711
00:52:56.005 --> 00:52:58.257
Ow!

712
00:52:59.759 --> 00:53:02.052
Bee-keek. beak-beak.

713
00:53:04.305 --> 00:53:05.723
Elphie. let's be honest.

714
00:53:06.307 --> 00:53:08.225
Your way hasn't worked.

715
00:53:08.309 --> 00:53:11.603
But if you join forces with us.
if people see that you're with us.

716
00:53:12.105 --> 00:53:13.731
they'll begin to trust you.

717
00:53:13.815 --> 00:53:15.608
You'll accomplish so much more.

718
00:53:15.692 --> 00:53:17.527
Yeah. Yeah. So much more.

719
00:53:17.610 --> 00:53:19.403
You know. we could be like a...
like a family.

720
00:53:19.487 --> 00:53:23.199
-You know. I've never really had a family.
-Lucky you.

721
00:53:23.282 --> 00:53:27.744
That's why I've wanted to give
the citizens of Oz... everything.

722
00:53:27.829 --> 00:53:30.331
-So you lied to them?
-No. No.

723
00:53:31.040 --> 00:53:32.708
No-- Well. um.

724
00:53:33.251 --> 00:53:35.670
only verbally.

725
00:53:36.963 --> 00:53:39.340
But those were the lies
that they wanted to hear.

726
00:53:40.341 --> 00:53:44.553
♪ <i>The truth is not a thing of
Fact or reason</i> ♪

727
00:53:46.013 --> 00:53:49.808
♪ <i>The truth is just
What everyone agrees on</i> ♪

728
00:53:51.269 --> 00:53:54.021
You see. back where I come from.
we got a whole lot of people

729
00:53:54.105 --> 00:53:56.607
who believe all sorts of things
that aren't true.

730
00:53:56.691 --> 00:53:58.025
You know what we call it?

731
00:53:59.527 --> 00:54:00.528
History.

732
00:54:01.738 --> 00:54:02.947
Ooh.

733
00:54:03.030 --> 00:54:05.449
♪ <i>A man's called a traitor</i> ♪

734
00:54:06.325 --> 00:54:07.993
♪ <i>Or liberator</i> ♪

735
00:54:08.077 --> 00:54:10.162
♪ <i>A rich man's a thief</i> ♪

736
00:54:10.246 --> 00:54:11.580
♪ <i>Or philanthropist</i> ♪

737
00:54:12.790 --> 00:54:15.250
♪ <i>Is one an invader</i> ♪

738
00:54:15.334 --> 00:54:17.627
♪ <i>Or noble crusader?</i> ♪

739
00:54:17.712 --> 00:54:22.007
♪ <i>It's all in which label
Is able to persist</i> ♪

740
00:54:22.508 --> 00:54:24.676
♪ <i>There are precious few at ease</i> ♪

741
00:54:24.761 --> 00:54:27.346
<i>With moral ambiguities</i>

742
00:54:27.430 --> 00:54:31.434
♪ <i>So we act as though they don't exist</i> ♪

743
00:54:35.521 --> 00:54:37.272
It's not my best pupil.

744
00:54:40.276 --> 00:54:44.405
♪ <i>They call him "Wonderful"</i> ♪

745
00:54:44.489 --> 00:54:46.949
♪ <i>So I am wonderful</i> ♪

746
00:54:47.033 --> 00:54:51.533
♪ <i>He is so wonderful
It's part of his name</i> ♪

747
00:54:52.413 --> 00:54:56.913
♪ <i>And with our help
You can be the same</i> ♪

748
00:55:03.007 --> 00:55:04.008
Come with me.

749
00:55:14.352 --> 00:55:17.104
Elphie. aren't you tired of running?

750
00:55:17.855 --> 00:55:19.273
Think of what we could do.

751
00:55:20.441 --> 00:55:21.608
Together.

752
00:55:27.698 --> 00:55:29.866
♪ <i>Unlimited</i> ♪

753
00:55:31.828 --> 00:55:36.040
♪ <i>Together we're unlimited</i> ♪

754
00:55:36.874 --> 00:55:41.374
♪ <i>Together we'll be the greatest team
There's ever been</i> ♪

755
00:55:42.004 --> 00:55:43.380
♪ <i>Elphie</i> ♪

756
00:55:43.464 --> 00:55:46.675
♪ <i>Dreams the way we planned 'em</i> ♪

757
00:55:47.260 --> 00:55:50.388
♪ <i>If we work in tandem</i> ♪

758
00:55:50.471 --> 00:55:54.600
♪ <i>There's no fight we cannot win</i> ♪

759
00:55:54.684 --> 00:55:57.728
♪ <i>At long. long. last
Receive your due</i> ♪

760
00:55:57.812 --> 00:56:00.189
♪ <i>Long overdue</i> ♪

761
00:56:00.273 --> 00:56:04.773
♪ <i>Elphaba. a celebration throughout Oz</i> ♪

762
00:56:05.778 --> 00:56:10.278
♪ <i>That's all to do with you</i> ♪

763
00:56:22.003 --> 00:56:24.338
♪ <i>Wonderful</i> ♪

764
00:56:24.422 --> 00:56:27.383
♪ <i>They'll call you "Wonderful"</i> ♪

765
00:56:27.466 --> 00:56:30.177
♪ <i>Come and be wonderful</i> ♪

766
00:56:30.261 --> 00:56:31.553
♪ <i>Trust me. it's fun!</i> ♪

767
00:56:32.847 --> 00:56:34.890
♪ <i>We will be wonderful</i> ♪

768
00:56:34.974 --> 00:56:37.768
♪ <i>You'll make me wonderful</i> ♪

769
00:56:38.436 --> 00:56:41.564
♪ <i>Wonderful! Wonderful!</i> ♪

770
00:57:12.553 --> 00:57:14.221
<i>Who are you?</i>

771
00:57:14.305 --> 00:57:18.767
<i>And why do you seek me?</i>

772
00:57:19.602 --> 00:57:20.603
Wait.

773
00:57:24.357 --> 00:57:28.235
♪ <i>It's possible I could agree</i> ♪

774
00:57:28.319 --> 00:57:30.070
♪ <i>Wonderful</i> ♪

775
00:57:30.571 --> 00:57:35.071
♪ <i>But this time
You have to prove yourself to me</i> ♪

776
00:57:38.746 --> 00:57:39.955
No more blaming the animals.

777
00:57:40.039 --> 00:57:43.042
And the ones who've left Oz
should be free to return without fear.

778
00:57:43.125 --> 00:57:44.668
Hey. with you by my side.

779
00:57:44.752 --> 00:57:47.045
I'm not going to need
to blame the animals anymore.

780
00:57:47.129 --> 00:57:50.715
You're not gonna need spies either. so...
set the monkeys free.

781
00:57:50.800 --> 00:57:52.551
Oh. yeah? Hang on. Hang on.

782
00:58:01.143 --> 00:58:02.811
Why? Why?

783
00:58:03.562 --> 00:58:06.439
I think I got it. I think got it. Um...

784
00:58:12.154 --> 00:58:13.155
Done.

785
00:58:13.239 --> 00:58:16.575
I did it. I mean. we did it.

786
00:58:17.827 --> 00:58:19.787
I'll see you two in a clock tick.

787
00:58:20.371 --> 00:58:24.333
Elphie. I'm so happy.

788
00:58:28.629 --> 00:58:30.631
I'm getting married.

789
00:58:31.966 --> 00:58:32.800
So.

790
00:58:33.050 --> 00:58:34.593
you want me to prove myself?

791
00:58:35.177 --> 00:58:37.679
Oh. my gosh. Look in your hand.

792
00:58:39.432 --> 00:58:40.766
How'd that get there?

793
00:58:41.267 --> 00:58:45.145
It's a key. It's a key.

794
00:58:45.229 --> 00:58:46.688
Aren't you surprised?

795
00:58:47.189 --> 00:58:49.107
I liked that dance. That was fun.

796
00:58:49.191 --> 00:58:50.650
Come here.

797
00:58:50.735 --> 00:58:54.155
Now...
...I've been keeping them locked in here.

798
00:58:54.238 --> 00:58:57.282
um. for their own safety.

799
00:59:00.036 --> 00:59:02.663
But no need for that anymore.

800
00:59:04.165 --> 00:59:05.291
Okay.

801
00:59:05.374 --> 00:59:07.793
Hey. wanna come over here
and do the honors?

802
00:59:07.877 --> 00:59:10.921
'Cause if you put that in here.
it'll let 'em go.

803
00:59:12.089 --> 00:59:13.799
And. uh. I...

804
00:59:13.883 --> 00:59:17.303
Gosh. I hope you feel good about
this whole thing 'cause. well. you've won.

805
00:59:17.386 --> 00:59:19.304
but I think we all have.

806
00:59:38.324 --> 00:59:39.325
Chistery.

807
00:59:43.245 --> 00:59:45.330
Nothing can change
what's been done to you.

808
00:59:47.583 --> 00:59:50.210
Well... what I've done.

809
00:59:52.004 --> 00:59:53.505
But at least you have your freedom now.

810
00:59:54.924 --> 00:59:56.467
Chistery. can you speak?

811
01:00:00.054 --> 01:00:01.138
Please try.

812
01:00:05.392 --> 01:00:06.393
Well.

813
01:00:07.728 --> 01:00:08.729
go on.

814
01:00:10.064 --> 01:00:11.065
You're free.

815
01:00:12.858 --> 01:00:14.025
Fly.

816
01:00:26.330 --> 01:00:27.331
Fly.

817
01:00:30.626 --> 01:00:31.918
Fly!

818
01:00:42.138 --> 01:00:43.139
Wonderful.

819
01:00:43.222 --> 01:00:45.182
Uh. well...

820
01:00:45.266 --> 01:00:49.353
Hey. if you and I are gonna go down there
and greet those fancy folks.

821
01:00:49.436 --> 01:00:51.396
I'd better spruce up.

822
01:01:13.878 --> 01:01:15.296
Chistery. what's wrong?

823
01:03:24.300 --> 01:03:25.342
Dr. Dillamond.

824
01:03:29.680 --> 01:03:32.265
Dr. Dillamond. can you speak?

825
01:03:32.975 --> 01:03:34.101
It's me. Elphaba.

826
01:03:44.111 --> 01:03:45.612
Let me explain.

827
01:03:45.696 --> 01:03:47.864
'cause this is not what it looks like.

828
01:03:51.452 --> 01:03:52.703
Elphaba.

829
01:03:52.786 --> 01:03:56.664
some animals cannot be trusted.

830
01:03:57.249 --> 01:03:58.250
Yes.

831
01:03:59.209 --> 01:04:00.335
I know that now.

832
01:04:05.924 --> 01:04:10.424
And these sacred vows
are to be entered into.

833
01:04:10.512 --> 01:04:14.599
not lightly. but merrily.

834
01:04:14.683 --> 01:04:15.684
Elphaba.

835
01:04:16.685 --> 01:04:17.686
try to understand.

836
01:04:18.437 --> 01:04:19.271
No.

837
01:04:20.773 --> 01:04:22.065
I'm not a bad man.

838
01:04:22.149 --> 01:04:23.316
-I'm just a--
-Yes. you are.

839
01:04:23.400 --> 01:04:25.110
You're a very bad man.

840
01:04:29.323 --> 01:04:32.534
You once asked me
what my heart's desire was.

841
01:04:32.618 --> 01:04:34.620
and I know now what that is.

842
01:04:36.914 --> 01:04:39.541
And that is to fight you
till the day I die.

843
01:04:47.466 --> 01:04:48.300
Run.

844
01:04:57.851 --> 01:05:00.270
And do you. Glinda...

845
01:05:03.023 --> 01:05:05.442
What is that horrendible sound?

846
01:05:21.250 --> 01:05:22.834
Move!

847
01:05:31.009 --> 01:05:32.301
Stay there.

848
01:05:37.724 --> 01:05:38.725
Fiyero!

849
01:05:52.197 --> 01:05:54.699
This is the work of the Wicked Witch.

850
01:05:54.783 --> 01:05:56.493
She wants to kill us all!

851
01:06:17.347 --> 01:06:18.765
No!

852
01:06:21.810 --> 01:06:24.187
How does it feel
to have your voice taken away?

853
01:06:26.064 --> 01:06:27.065
Silence. Witch.

854
01:06:31.278 --> 01:06:32.153
Water.

855
01:06:32.237 --> 01:06:35.198
-Lots of it. Bring water!
-Sir.

856
01:06:35.282 --> 01:06:36.741
As much as you can carry.

857
01:06:37.367 --> 01:06:38.534
A little help?

858
01:06:47.002 --> 01:06:48.003
Please.

859
01:06:50.964 --> 01:06:51.965
Thank you.

860
01:06:52.674 --> 01:06:54.425
That was unpleasant.

861
01:06:57.971 --> 01:07:01.224
Well. I think my trachea is otherwi--

862
01:07:01.808 --> 01:07:03.309
What? What are you doing?

863
01:07:03.393 --> 01:07:05.311
-Shush. you. Get in.
-What?

864
01:07:05.896 --> 01:07:06.813
Get in.

865
01:07:08.190 --> 01:07:10.775
Unless you want the guests
to know the truth about their wizard.

866
01:07:12.486 --> 01:07:14.488
-Get in!
-Yes. yes.

867
01:07:36.343 --> 01:07:37.635
Your Ozness!

868
01:07:38.428 --> 01:07:39.971
Fiyero? What are you...

869
01:07:40.931 --> 01:07:42.807
What is happening?

870
01:07:42.891 --> 01:07:45.810
What's happened is that
these two traitors--

871
01:07:45.894 --> 01:07:47.520
Not another word. Your Ozness.

872
01:07:47.604 --> 01:07:49.939
Darling. have you misplaced your mind?

873
01:07:50.023 --> 01:07:50.982
What are you doing?

874
01:08:07.207 --> 01:08:08.333
I'm going with her.

875
01:08:09.418 --> 01:08:10.961
-What?
-What?

876
01:08:13.797 --> 01:08:15.673
-Let's go.
-What?

877
01:08:15.757 --> 01:08:17.008
-Let's go.
-Wait.

878
01:08:17.092 --> 01:08:18.134
What?

879
01:08:19.386 --> 01:08:23.139
You mean to tell me that the two of you...

880
01:08:23.932 --> 01:08:24.933
This whole time?

881
01:08:25.017 --> 01:08:26.685
No. It wasn't like that.

882
01:08:26.768 --> 01:08:27.727
Go.

883
01:08:30.439 --> 01:08:31.440
Now.

884
01:08:38.405 --> 01:08:39.948
You deserve each other.

885
01:08:45.078 --> 01:08:46.245
You frightened me.

886
01:08:47.497 --> 01:08:49.248
For a while there.
I thought you changed.

887
01:08:55.047 --> 01:08:56.173
I have changed.

888
01:09:05.390 --> 01:09:07.392
This dulls the pain.
if you want a swig?

889
01:09:12.856 --> 01:09:17.356
No. no. no. no! No! No!

890
01:09:18.278 --> 01:09:19.487
We've got the water.
Madame.

891
01:09:19.571 --> 01:09:22.615
Fools! You're too late. Get out!

892
01:09:24.076 --> 01:09:25.494
How could you let this happen?

893
01:09:25.577 --> 01:09:27.370
Uh. do you have a hairpin?

894
01:09:28.538 --> 01:09:29.914
Thanks.

895
01:09:29.998 --> 01:09:32.375
Uh. she and I had a deal.

896
01:09:33.251 --> 01:09:34.252
But...

897
01:09:36.046 --> 01:09:37.338
she double-crossed me.

898
01:09:39.091 --> 01:09:42.511
We must smoke her out.
force her to show herself.

899
01:09:43.679 --> 01:09:46.264
Without the monkeys.
I don't know how we're gonna do that.

900
01:09:48.225 --> 01:09:49.267
Her sister.

901
01:09:51.770 --> 01:09:52.979
Use her sister.

902
01:09:55.565 --> 01:09:56.649
Spread a rumor

903
01:09:58.151 --> 01:09:59.652
that her sister's in trouble.

904
01:10:00.737 --> 01:10:02.572
She'll fly to her side.
and you'll have her.

905
01:10:06.451 --> 01:10:09.704
Now. if you'll excuse me.
I need to lie down.

906
01:10:09.788 --> 01:10:10.997
I have a bit of a headache.

907
01:10:13.041 --> 01:10:14.792
A rumor won't do.

908
01:10:16.253 --> 01:10:18.463
Elphaba's too smart. That's right.

909
01:10:18.547 --> 01:10:21.299
These things must be done delicately.

910
01:10:22.426 --> 01:10:23.427
Perhaps...

911
01:10:24.803 --> 01:10:26.721
a change in the weather.

912
01:10:46.658 --> 01:10:47.742
♪ <i>Don't wish</i> ♪

913
01:10:49.786 --> 01:10:50.953
♪ <i>Don't start</i> ♪

914
01:10:52.873 --> 01:10:57.373
♪ <i>Wishing only wounds the heart</i> ♪

915
01:11:05.886 --> 01:11:10.056
♪ <i>There's a girl I know</i> ♪

916
01:11:12.267 --> 01:11:14.936
♪ <i>He loves her so</i> ♪

917
01:11:21.276 --> 01:11:25.776
♪ <i>I'm not that... girl</i> ♪

918
01:13:01.793 --> 01:13:05.254
♪ <i>Kiss me too fiercely</i> ♪

919
01:13:05.338 --> 01:13:07.715
♪ <i>Hold me too tight</i> ♪

920
01:13:07.799 --> 01:13:11.719
♪ <i>I need help believing</i> ♪

921
01:13:11.803 --> 01:13:16.303
♪ <i>You're with me tonight!</i> ♪

922
01:13:17.350 --> 01:13:21.850
♪ <i>My wildest dreamings
Could not foresee</i> ♪

923
01:13:24.065 --> 01:13:27.234
♪ <i>Lying beside you</i> ♪

924
01:13:27.319 --> 01:13:31.406
♪ <i>With you wanting me</i> ♪

925
01:13:31.907 --> 01:13:35.535
♪ <i>Just for this moment</i> ♪

926
01:13:35.619 --> 01:13:39.247
♪ <i>As long as you're mine</i> ♪

927
01:13:39.331 --> 01:13:43.831
♪ <i>I've lost all resistance</i> ♪

928
01:13:44.294 --> 01:13:47.547
♪ <i>And crossed some borderline</i> ♪

929
01:13:47.631 --> 01:13:51.259
♪ <i>And if it turns out</i> ♪

930
01:13:51.343 --> 01:13:55.722
♪ <i>It's over too fast.</i> ♪

931
01:13:55.805 --> 01:14:00.305
♪ <i>I'll make every last moment last</i> ♪

932
01:14:03.063 --> 01:14:07.563
♪ <i>As long as you're mine</i> ♪

933
01:14:15.033 --> 01:14:16.242
You're beautiful.

934
01:14:17.494 --> 01:14:19.746
You don't have to lie to me.

935
01:14:31.800 --> 01:14:32.884
It's not lying.

936
01:14:35.637 --> 01:14:38.097
-It's...
-What is it?

937
01:14:39.265 --> 01:14:41.058
It's looking at things another way.

938
01:14:43.937 --> 01:14:48.437
♪ <i>Maybe I'm brainless
Maybe I'm wise</i> ♪

939
01:14:50.276 --> 01:14:53.362
♪ <i>But you've got me seeing</i> ♪

940
01:14:53.446 --> 01:14:57.946
♪ <i>Through different eyes</i> ♪

941
01:14:59.828 --> 01:15:04.328
♪ <i>Somehow I've fallen
Under your spell</i> ♪

942
01:15:06.001 --> 01:15:09.671
♪ <i>And somehow I'm feeling</i> ♪

943
01:15:09.754 --> 01:15:14.091
♪ <i>It's up that I fell</i> ♪

944
01:15:14.175 --> 01:15:17.761
♪ <i>Every moment</i> ♪

945
01:15:17.846 --> 01:15:21.474
♪ <i>As long as you're mine</i> ♪

946
01:15:21.558 --> 01:15:26.058
♪ <i>I'll wake up my body</i> ♪

947
01:15:26.604 --> 01:15:29.732
♪ <i>And make up for lost time</i> ♪

948
01:15:29.816 --> 01:15:33.486
♪ <i>Say there's no future</i> ♪

949
01:15:33.570 --> 01:15:37.949
♪ <i>For us as a pair</i> ♪

950
01:15:38.033 --> 01:15:41.911
♪ <i>And though I may know</i> ♪

951
01:15:41.995 --> 01:15:46.495
♪ <i>I don't care</i> ♪

952
01:15:49.294 --> 01:15:53.214
♪ <i>Just for this moment</i> ♪

953
01:15:53.298 --> 01:15:57.176
♪ <i>As long as you're mine</i> ♪

954
01:15:57.260 --> 01:16:01.639
♪ <i>Come be how you want to</i> ♪

955
01:16:02.390 --> 01:16:05.267
♪ <i>And see how bright we shine</i> ♪

956
01:16:05.351 --> 01:16:08.979
♪ <i>Borrow the moonlight</i> ♪

957
01:16:09.064 --> 01:16:13.564
♪ <i>Until it is through</i> ♪

958
01:16:17.655 --> 01:16:22.155
♪ <i>And know I'll be here
Holding you</i> ♪

959
01:16:28.750 --> 01:16:33.250
♪ <i>As long as you're mine</i> ♪

960
01:16:43.807 --> 01:16:44.808
What is it?

961
01:16:44.891 --> 01:16:45.892
It's just...

962
01:16:46.476 --> 01:16:50.062
For the first time. I feel... wicked.

963
01:17:44.159 --> 01:17:46.536
-Take cover!
-Get inside!

964
01:17:46.619 --> 01:17:48.078
Gather all your things!

965
01:17:48.163 --> 01:17:49.873
Run home! Go!

966
01:18:10.185 --> 01:18:12.353
Boq! Boq!

967
01:18:12.937 --> 01:18:14.104
Where are you?

968
01:18:15.398 --> 01:18:17.316
Come on! Come on! Inside!

969
01:18:17.400 --> 01:18:18.567
Stay calm.

970
01:18:18.651 --> 01:18:20.486
Move! Go!

971
01:18:22.030 --> 01:18:23.031
Boq!

972
01:18:36.628 --> 01:18:38.421
You can't go on living here.

973
01:18:39.255 --> 01:18:40.923
-They'll find you.
-I'll be all right.

974
01:18:41.758 --> 01:18:42.759
Listen.

975
01:18:44.469 --> 01:18:46.929
My family has a castle in Kiamo Ko.

976
01:18:47.013 --> 01:18:48.305
Never lived in it.

977
01:18:48.389 --> 01:18:49.473
W-Where do you live?

978
01:18:50.934 --> 01:18:52.018
In the other castle.

979
01:18:52.769 --> 01:18:54.937
Okay. Of course.

980
01:18:55.021 --> 01:18:57.732
I mean. it's the perfect hideout.
There's tunnels. secret passageways.

981
01:18:59.442 --> 01:19:00.693
You'll be safer there.

982
01:19:03.112 --> 01:19:04.196
<i>Boq!</i>

983
01:19:05.490 --> 01:19:06.657
<i>Where are you?</i>

984
01:19:06.741 --> 01:19:07.992
What?

985
01:19:08.076 --> 01:19:09.494
<i>Boq!</i>

986
01:19:10.954 --> 01:19:12.163
<i>Boq!</i>

987
01:19:13.539 --> 01:19:14.581
What is it?

988
01:19:15.792 --> 01:19:16.793
What's wrong?

989
01:19:20.380 --> 01:19:22.548
This isn't gonna make any sense. but...

990
01:19:25.093 --> 01:19:26.302
There's a house...

991
01:19:28.721 --> 01:19:30.139
and it's flying through the sky.

992
01:19:34.102 --> 01:19:36.312
<i>Boq!</i>

993
01:19:36.396 --> 01:19:38.189
<i>Boq!</i>

994
01:19:41.276 --> 01:19:44.153
Hey. Hey. Hey.

995
01:19:44.946 --> 01:19:47.323
My sister. She's in danger.
I have to get to her.

996
01:19:47.407 --> 01:19:48.741
What? I'm coming with you.

997
01:19:48.825 --> 01:19:51.160
No. It's too dangerous.

998
01:19:55.498 --> 01:19:56.957
Will we ever see each other again?

999
01:20:01.254 --> 01:20:05.299
Elphaba. we are going
to be together always.

1000
01:20:07.343 --> 01:20:11.347
You can see houses flying through the sky.
but you can't see that?

1001
01:21:38.726 --> 01:21:39.727
This way. dear.

1002
01:21:39.811 --> 01:21:41.854
Goodbye. Dorothy. Bye. Dodo.

1003
01:21:41.938 --> 01:21:44.273
It's just that one road the whole time.

1004
01:21:46.234 --> 01:21:47.944
Take your time. Hurry up. darling.

1005
01:22:20.226 --> 01:22:21.477
Goodbye. Nessa.

1006
01:22:32.738 --> 01:22:34.322
What a touching display of grief.

1007
01:22:34.407 --> 01:22:35.533
Oh. shiz.

1008
01:22:36.742 --> 01:22:37.617
I scare you?

1009
01:22:38.995 --> 01:22:40.663
I seem to have that effect on people.

1010
01:22:42.540 --> 01:22:46.210
I would appreciate a moment
to say goodbye to my sister. Alone.

1011
01:22:47.712 --> 01:22:48.546
Of course.

1012
01:23:05.438 --> 01:23:06.564
Oh. Nessa.

1013
01:23:09.400 --> 01:23:10.401
Forgive me.

1014
01:23:11.527 --> 01:23:13.529
Oh. Elphaba. don't blame yourself. please.

1015
01:23:13.613 --> 01:23:15.239
It's dreadful. it is.

1016
01:23:16.032 --> 01:23:19.535
I mean... to have a house fall on you...

1017
01:23:20.536 --> 01:23:24.039
But accidents will happen. And...

1018
01:23:29.045 --> 01:23:30.629
You call that an accident?

1019
01:23:32.173 --> 01:23:35.593
You think cyclones just appear
out of the blue?

1020
01:23:36.219 --> 01:23:38.429
I don't know.
I never really thought about it--

1021
01:23:38.513 --> 01:23:41.474
And how dare you send that
mulish farm girl off to see the Wizard.

1022
01:23:41.557 --> 01:23:43.183
as if he could do anything to help?

1023
01:23:43.267 --> 01:23:45.018
She's lost. She's far from home.

1024
01:23:45.102 --> 01:23:46.311
She took a dead woman's shoes.

1025
01:23:46.395 --> 01:23:48.188
I had to do something.

1026
01:23:48.272 --> 01:23:50.274
I'm a public figure now.
People expect me to--

1027
01:23:50.358 --> 01:23:51.317
Lie?

1028
01:23:51.901 --> 01:23:53.444
Be encouraging.

1029
01:23:53.528 --> 01:23:56.113
Those shoes
are all I have left of my sister.

1030
01:23:56.197 --> 01:23:57.573
They weren't yours to give.

1031
01:24:01.285 --> 01:24:02.494
Yes. well.

1032
01:24:02.578 --> 01:24:05.914
it seems a lot of us are taking things
that don't belong to us now. aren't we?

1033
01:24:08.417 --> 01:24:10.252
Now. you just wait a clock tick.

1034
01:24:10.836 --> 01:24:12.420
It might be hard for you to comprehend

1035
01:24:12.505 --> 01:24:16.008
that someone like him
could choose someone like me.

1036
01:24:16.592 --> 01:24:18.468
but it's happened and it's real.

1037
01:24:19.512 --> 01:24:22.264
And you can wave that ridiculous wand
all you want.

1038
01:24:22.348 --> 01:24:23.307
You can't change it.

1039
01:24:24.767 --> 01:24:26.518
He never belonged to you.

1040
01:24:26.602 --> 01:24:27.936
He doesn't love you.

1041
01:24:29.105 --> 01:24:30.147
He never did.

1042
01:24:30.982 --> 01:24:33.401
He loves me.

1043
01:24:33.985 --> 01:24:34.986
Oh. my...

1044
01:24:43.452 --> 01:24:44.453
Feel better?

1045
01:24:45.288 --> 01:24:46.580
I do.

1046
01:24:46.664 --> 01:24:47.665
Good.

1047
01:24:51.919 --> 01:24:53.211
Me too.

1048
01:24:58.467 --> 01:24:59.551
Are you crazy?

1049
01:25:01.137 --> 01:25:03.305
Excuse me. what do you think you're doing?

1050
01:25:04.890 --> 01:25:06.808
Come on! Come on! Bring it!

1051
01:25:06.892 --> 01:25:07.851
Get back!

1052
01:25:13.399 --> 01:25:14.566
Get--

1053
01:25:15.151 --> 01:25:17.194
Here. Let's go!

1054
01:25:19.739 --> 01:25:20.865
You...

1055
01:25:23.117 --> 01:25:25.327
Please.

1056
01:25:26.078 --> 01:25:27.788
Where'd you get that?

1057
01:25:33.169 --> 01:25:34.336
What are you doing?

1058
01:25:39.800 --> 01:25:41.843
Come on. Let's go. greenie.

1059
01:25:41.927 --> 01:25:43.094
Use your hands.

1060
01:25:44.138 --> 01:25:45.097
Come on.

1061
01:25:45.681 --> 01:25:47.683
-Come on. Bring it on.
-Are you out of your mind?

1062
01:25:47.767 --> 01:25:48.893
-No.
-Get off of me.

1063
01:25:48.976 --> 01:25:50.268
Attention!

1064
01:25:50.353 --> 01:25:51.604
Halt in the name of the Wizard!

1065
01:25:51.687 --> 01:25:53.146
-Off of me.
-Let her go.

1066
01:25:53.230 --> 01:25:55.690
No. no. no. I almost had her.
I almost had her.

1067
01:25:56.317 --> 01:25:57.443
I almost had her.

1068
01:25:58.235 --> 01:25:59.402
Easy.

1069
01:25:59.487 --> 01:26:01.989
Sorry it took us so long to get here.
Your Goodness.

1070
01:26:04.742 --> 01:26:05.909
You were a part of this?

1071
01:26:06.494 --> 01:26:07.453
Elphaba. no--

1072
01:26:07.536 --> 01:26:10.539
I can't believe you would stoop so low
as to use my sister's death to capture me.

1073
01:26:10.623 --> 01:26:12.291
I never meant it to get this far. I--

1074
01:26:12.375 --> 01:26:15.211
Let the green girl go.

1075
01:26:16.504 --> 01:26:19.673
Else explain to all Oz
how the Wizard's guards watched

1076
01:26:19.757 --> 01:26:21.592
while Glinda the Good was slain.

1077
01:26:24.011 --> 01:26:24.970
What?

1078
01:26:38.317 --> 01:26:39.568
-Elphaba. go.
-No.

1079
01:26:39.652 --> 01:26:41.528
-Not without you.
-Go!

1080
01:26:43.364 --> 01:26:44.239
Go.

1081
01:26:45.074 --> 01:26:45.908
I...

1082
01:26:48.452 --> 01:26:49.453
Now.

1083
01:26:52.998 --> 01:26:53.999
Go.

1084
01:27:11.892 --> 01:27:13.184
Please. protect her.

1085
01:27:43.883 --> 01:27:46.302
No. you're hurting him.
Stop it now.

1086
01:27:46.385 --> 01:27:48.595
Stop. In the name of Goodness. stop.

1087
01:27:51.724 --> 01:27:54.268
Can't you see he wasn't going to
harm me? He just...

1088
01:27:59.690 --> 01:28:00.857
He loves her.

1089
01:28:00.941 --> 01:28:02.943
Glinda. I am so sorry.

1090
01:28:03.694 --> 01:28:06.113
-Take him out to that field.
-What? No. Please.

1091
01:28:06.197 --> 01:28:09.200
Put him up on those poles
till he tells us where the Witch went.

1092
01:28:09.283 --> 01:28:11.493
Fiyero! No. Please. Let go of me.

1093
01:28:11.577 --> 01:28:14.997
Fiyero. Fiyero!

1094
01:28:48.197 --> 01:28:51.825
♪ <i>Let his flesh not be torn
Let his blood leave no stain</i> ♪

1095
01:28:51.909 --> 01:28:55.621
♪ <i>Though they beat him
Let him feel no pain</i> ♪

1096
01:28:56.497 --> 01:28:58.332
♪ <i>Let his bones never break</i> ♪

1097
01:28:58.415 --> 01:29:01.292
♪ <i>And however they try
To destroy him</i> ♪

1098
01:29:01.377 --> 01:29:05.877
♪ <i>Let him never die
Let him never die</i> ♪

1099
01:29:16.517 --> 01:29:18.560
What good is this chanting?

1100
01:29:18.644 --> 01:29:20.354
I don't even know what I'm reading.

1101
01:29:20.437 --> 01:29:24.232
♪ <i>I don't even know what trick
I ought to try</i> ♪

1102
01:29:24.316 --> 01:29:27.902
♪ <i>Fiyero. where are you?
Already dead. or bleeding?</i> ♪

1103
01:29:27.987 --> 01:29:32.487
♪ <i>One more disaster
I can add to my generous supply?</i> ♪

1104
01:29:42.835 --> 01:29:47.089
♪ <i>No good deed goes unpunished</i> ♪

1105
01:29:47.631 --> 01:29:51.635
♪ <i>No act of charity goes unresented</i> ♪

1106
01:29:51.719 --> 01:29:56.219
♪ <i>No good deed goes unpunished
That's my new creed</i> ♪

1107
01:29:57.725 --> 01:30:02.225
♪ <i>My road of good intentions led
Where such roads always lead</i> ♪

1108
01:30:03.397 --> 01:30:07.897
♪ <i>No good deed
Goes unpunished</i> ♪

1109
01:30:16.160 --> 01:30:17.161
Nessa?

1110
01:30:19.997 --> 01:30:21.331
Dr. Dillamond.

1111
01:30:24.168 --> 01:30:27.045
♪ <i>Fiyero</i> ♪

1112
01:30:27.963 --> 01:30:32.463
♪ <i>Fiyero</i> ♪

1113
01:30:37.306 --> 01:30:39.808
♪ <i>One question haunts and hurts
Too much</i> ♪

1114
01:30:39.892 --> 01:30:41.852
♪ <i>Too much to mention</i> ♪

1115
01:30:41.936 --> 01:30:46.436
♪ <i>Was I really seeking good
Or just seeking attention?</i> ♪

1116
01:30:46.565 --> 01:30:51.065
♪ <i>Is that all good deeds are
When looked at with an ice-cold eye?</i> ♪

1117
01:30:51.779 --> 01:30:56.279
♪ <i>If that's all good deeds are
Maybe that's the reason why.</i> ♪

1118
01:31:01.205 --> 01:31:05.334
♪ <i>No good deed goes unpunished</i> ♪

1119
01:31:05.417 --> 01:31:09.712
♪ <i>All helpful urges
Should be circumvented</i> ♪

1120
01:31:09.797 --> 01:31:13.801
♪ <i>No good deed goes unpunished</i> ♪

1121
01:31:13.884 --> 01:31:18.384
♪ <i>Sure. I meant well
Well. look at what well-meant did</i> ♪

1122
01:31:18.931 --> 01:31:21.183
All right. enough! So be it.

1123
01:31:21.767 --> 01:31:22.768
♪ <i>So be it. then</i> ♪

1124
01:31:25.729 --> 01:31:30.229
♪ <i>Let all Oz be agreed
I'm wicked through and through</i> ♪

1125
01:31:31.026 --> 01:31:34.988
♪ <i>And since I can't succeed
Fiyero. saving you</i> ♪

1126
01:31:35.072 --> 01:31:39.572
♪ <i>I promise no good deed
Will I attempt to do again</i> ♪

1127
01:31:40.244 --> 01:31:43.121
♪ <i>Ever again</i> ♪

1128
01:31:43.205 --> 01:31:47.705
♪ <i>No good deed will I do</i> ♪

1129
01:31:49.837 --> 01:31:54.337
♪ <i>Again</i> ♪

1130
01:32:17.614 --> 01:32:19.032
You have visitors.

1131
01:32:19.116 --> 01:32:21.284
A girl from the land of Kansas.

1132
01:32:21.368 --> 01:32:23.661
and three friends
she picked up along the way.

1133
01:32:23.746 --> 01:32:26.081
A man made of tin. another made of straw.

1134
01:32:26.165 --> 01:32:28.417
And a very nervous lion.

1135
01:32:28.959 --> 01:32:31.628
They all want something they don't have.
of course.

1136
01:32:31.712 --> 01:32:32.879
I'm not seeing anybody.

1137
01:32:34.214 --> 01:32:36.966
But these are visitors we can use.

1138
01:32:52.900 --> 01:32:56.987
Bring me the broomstick
of the Wicked Witch of the West...

1139
01:32:58.113 --> 01:33:02.613
...so I have proof that she's dead.

1140
01:33:31.355 --> 01:33:34.107
♪ <i>Go and hunt her
And find her</i> ♪

1141
01:33:34.191 --> 01:33:35.942
♪ <i>And kill her</i> ♪

1142
01:33:36.485 --> 01:33:37.486
Kill her!

1143
01:33:38.779 --> 01:33:41.615
♪ <i>Go and hunt her
And find her</i> ♪

1144
01:33:41.698 --> 01:33:43.324
♪ <i>And kill her</i> ♪

1145
01:33:43.408 --> 01:33:46.369
Kill her! Kill her! Kill her!

1146
01:33:46.453 --> 01:33:49.205
♪ <i>Go and hunt her
And find her</i> ♪

1147
01:33:49.289 --> 01:33:51.165
♪ <i>And kill her</i> ♪

1148
01:33:51.250 --> 01:33:53.835
Melt her! Melt her!

1149
01:33:53.919 --> 01:33:56.922
♪ <i>Wickedness must be punished</i> ♪

1150
01:33:57.005 --> 01:33:58.339
Kill her!

1151
01:33:58.423 --> 01:34:02.343
♪ <i>Evil effectively eliminated</i> ♪

1152
01:34:02.427 --> 01:34:06.097
♪ <i>Wickedness must be punished</i> ♪

1153
01:34:06.181 --> 01:34:07.056
♪ <i>Kill the Witch!</i> ♪

1154
01:34:07.141 --> 01:34:07.975
Kill her!

1155
01:34:08.058 --> 01:34:09.059
♪ <i>Melt her</i> ♪

1156
01:34:09.143 --> 01:34:11.186
♪ <i>Melt the Witch</i> ♪

1157
01:34:11.979 --> 01:34:14.564
And this is more than just a service
to the Wizard.

1158
01:34:14.648 --> 01:34:16.941
I've a personal score to settle
with Elph--

1159
01:34:18.026 --> 01:34:19.569
with the Witch!

1160
01:34:20.821 --> 01:34:24.491
♪ <i>It's due to her I'm made of tin
Her spell made this occur</i> ♪

1161
01:34:24.992 --> 01:34:27.160
♪ <i>So for once I'm glad I'm heartless</i> ♪

1162
01:34:27.244 --> 01:34:29.037
♪ <i>I'll be heartless killing her!</i> ♪

1163
01:34:31.832 --> 01:34:33.667
And I'm not the only one.

1164
01:34:34.877 --> 01:34:37.921
Tell them. Tell them what she did to you.

1165
01:34:39.506 --> 01:34:43.551
How you were just a cub...
and she cub-napped you.

1166
01:34:44.761 --> 01:34:48.389
♪ <i>You see. the Lion also
Has a grievance to repay</i> ♪

1167
01:34:48.473 --> 01:34:51.601
♪ <i>If she'd let him fight his own battles
When he was young</i> ♪

1168
01:34:51.685 --> 01:34:56.185
♪ <i>He wouldn't be a coward today</i> ♪

1169
01:35:00.277 --> 01:35:02.779
♪ <i>Go and hunt her
And find her</i> ♪

1170
01:35:02.863 --> 01:35:04.322
♪ <i>And kill her</i> ♪

1171
01:35:04.406 --> 01:35:07.617
Kill her! Kill her! Kill her!

1172
01:35:07.701 --> 01:35:08.743
Kill her!

1173
01:35:49.159 --> 01:35:50.160
Look.

1174
01:35:51.578 --> 01:35:56.078
♪ <i>There's that beautiful girl</i> ♪

1175
01:35:58.669 --> 01:36:01.838
♪ <i>With the beautiful life</i> ♪

1176
01:36:01.922 --> 01:36:06.422
♪ <i>Such a beautiful life
Built on lies</i> ♪

1177
01:36:08.762 --> 01:36:13.262
♪ <i>'Cause all that's required
To live in a dream</i> ♪

1178
01:36:15.644 --> 01:36:20.144
♪ <i>Is endlessly closing your eyes</i> ♪

1179
01:36:20.816 --> 01:36:25.316
♪ <i>She spins such beautiful stories</i> ♪

1180
01:36:26.613 --> 01:36:29.032
♪ <i>To sing her to sleep</i> ♪

1181
01:36:29.533 --> 01:36:34.033
♪ <i>Full of magic and glory and love</i> ♪

1182
01:36:35.372 --> 01:36:39.872
♪ <i>She's the girl in the bubble
The bright. shiny bubble</i> ♪

1183
01:36:43.213 --> 01:36:47.713
♪ <i>Blissfully floating above</i> ♪

1184
01:36:52.681 --> 01:36:56.851
♪ <i>But the truth has a way</i> ♪

1185
01:36:56.935 --> 01:37:00.063
♪ <i>Of seeping on in</i> ♪

1186
01:37:00.147 --> 01:37:04.647
♪ <i>Beneath the surface and sheen</i> ♪

1187
01:37:04.985 --> 01:37:09.485
♪ <i>And blind as you try to be</i> ♪

1188
01:37:09.614 --> 01:37:12.533
♪ <i>Eventually</i> ♪

1189
01:37:12.617 --> 01:37:17.117
♪ <i>It's hard to unsee what you've seen</i> ♪

1190
01:37:17.914 --> 01:37:22.414
♪ <i>And so that beautiful girl</i> ♪

1191
01:37:23.295 --> 01:37:26.214
♪ <i>With the beautiful life</i> ♪

1192
01:37:26.298 --> 01:37:30.798
♪ <i>Has a question that haunts her somehow</i> ♪

1193
01:37:31.470 --> 01:37:35.970
♪ <i>If she comes down from the sky
Gives the real world a try</i> ♪

1194
01:37:39.061 --> 01:37:42.606
♪ <i>Who in the world is she now?</i> ♪

1195
01:37:43.440 --> 01:37:47.940
♪ <i>And though so much of her wishes</i> ♪

1196
01:37:49.279 --> 01:37:51.948
♪ <i>That she could float on</i> ♪

1197
01:37:52.032 --> 01:37:56.532
♪ <i>And the beautiful lies never stop</i> ♪

1198
01:37:57.996 --> 01:38:02.291
♪ <i>For the girl in the bubble</i> ♪

1199
01:38:02.376 --> 01:38:05.545
♪ <i>The pink. shiny bubble</i> ♪

1200
01:38:05.629 --> 01:38:09.883
♪ <i>It's time for her bubble to pop</i> ♪

1201
01:38:15.597 --> 01:38:20.097
♪ <i>For the popular girl</i> ♪

1202
01:38:20.602 --> 01:38:25.102
♪ <i>High in the bubble</i> ♪

1203
01:38:40.872 --> 01:38:44.834
♪ <i>Isn't it high time</i> ♪

1204
01:38:46.628 --> 01:38:49.922
♪ <i>For her bubble</i> ♪

1205
01:38:52.509 --> 01:38:55.512
♪ <i>To pop?</i> ♪

1206
01:39:13.864 --> 01:39:16.741
Madame. we have got to stop this.
It's gone too far.

1207
01:39:17.325 --> 01:39:19.243
I think Elphaba can take care of herself.

1208
01:39:23.582 --> 01:39:24.499
Madame.

1209
01:39:27.836 --> 01:39:29.295
Something has been troubling me.

1210
01:39:32.716 --> 01:39:35.051
About Nessa and that cyclone.

1211
01:39:38.555 --> 01:39:39.556
Sad.

1212
01:39:40.682 --> 01:39:42.600
I suppose it was just her time.

1213
01:39:47.355 --> 01:39:48.481
Was it?

1214
01:39:52.819 --> 01:39:54.654
Was it? Or did you do--

1215
01:39:54.738 --> 01:39:57.782
Now. you listen to me. missy.

1216
01:39:57.866 --> 01:40:00.285
You may be fooling the rest of Oz.

1217
01:40:00.368 --> 01:40:02.286
but you're not fooling me.

1218
01:40:02.370 --> 01:40:06.332
You wanted this from the beginning.
"Galinda."

1219
01:40:06.416 --> 01:40:09.919
And now you're getting what you wanted.

1220
01:40:10.003 --> 01:40:13.297
-No. No.
-So just do what you do best.

1221
01:40:13.381 --> 01:40:15.758
Smile. Wave.

1222
01:40:18.929 --> 01:40:21.014
And shut up.

1223
01:41:00.428 --> 01:41:02.012
I need your help.

1224
01:41:09.854 --> 01:41:14.233
♪ <i>Wickedness must be punished</i> ♪

1225
01:41:14.317 --> 01:41:17.778
♪ <i>Brave Witch Hunters
I would join you if I could</i> ♪

1226
01:41:17.862 --> 01:41:22.362
♪ <i>Because Wickedness must be punished</i> ♪

1227
01:41:22.534 --> 01:41:24.577
♪ <i>Punished</i> ♪

1228
01:41:24.661 --> 01:41:28.498
♪ <i>Punished</i> ♪

1229
01:41:28.582 --> 01:41:33.082
♪ <i>But good</i> ♪

1230
01:41:34.087 --> 01:41:36.172
Monkeys.

1231
01:41:36.256 --> 01:41:40.756
Find that Dorothy
and bring back my sister's shoes.

1232
01:42:11.333 --> 01:42:14.044
Oh. for Oz's sake. stop crying.

1233
01:42:14.127 --> 01:42:15.545
I can't listen to it anymore.

1234
01:42:15.629 --> 01:42:17.422
You want to get home
and see your Aunt what's-her-name again?

1235
01:42:17.505 --> 01:42:20.633
-Then get those shoes off your feet!
-Please stop. I'm so sorry.

1236
01:42:22.135 --> 01:42:23.719
I wanna go home.

1237
01:42:26.014 --> 01:42:27.348
They're coming for you.

1238
01:42:29.934 --> 01:42:31.602
Let the little girl go.

1239
01:42:32.437 --> 01:42:33.479
Go away.

1240
01:42:35.065 --> 01:42:37.233
Elphaba. you can't go on like this.

1241
01:42:37.317 --> 01:42:38.568
I can do whatever I want.

1242
01:42:38.652 --> 01:42:39.819
Haven't you heard?

1243
01:42:41.488 --> 01:42:43.031
I'm the Wicked Witch of the West.

1244
01:42:48.411 --> 01:42:49.578
Chistery. at last.

1245
01:42:50.538 --> 01:42:51.997
What took you so long?

1246
01:42:52.082 --> 01:42:53.083
What is this?

1247
01:43:01.132 --> 01:43:02.800
Elphie. what is that?

1248
01:43:08.723 --> 01:43:09.932
It's Fiyero. isn't it?

1249
01:43:15.105 --> 01:43:16.106
Is he...

1250
01:43:21.444 --> 01:43:23.070
We've seen his face for the last time.

1251
01:43:23.613 --> 01:43:26.032
Oh. no.

1252
01:43:36.751 --> 01:43:37.752
You're right.

1253
01:43:39.629 --> 01:43:40.796
It's time.

1254
01:43:45.009 --> 01:43:46.010
I surrender.

1255
01:43:47.762 --> 01:43:48.596
What?

1256
01:43:49.389 --> 01:43:50.390
Wait.

1257
01:43:56.771 --> 01:43:57.980
Elphaba. what are you doing?

1258
01:43:58.064 --> 01:43:59.732
Glinda. you can't be found here with me.

1259
01:43:59.816 --> 01:44:01.734
-You must go.
-Elphie. no.

1260
01:44:01.818 --> 01:44:03.444
Please. you must now.

1261
01:44:03.528 --> 01:44:04.529
Fine.

1262
01:44:05.029 --> 01:44:06.739
I'll go and I'll tell everyone
the truth about you.

1263
01:44:06.823 --> 01:44:08.199
that you're not who they say you are.

1264
01:44:08.283 --> 01:44:09.534
No. you can't.

1265
01:44:10.118 --> 01:44:11.869
-Bu--
-They'll just turn against you.

1266
01:44:11.953 --> 01:44:13.913
-Well. I don't care.
-Well. I do.

1267
01:44:15.832 --> 01:44:18.042
I need you to promise that
you won't try to clear my name.

1268
01:44:18.126 --> 01:44:19.961
No. What? Why would I do that?

1269
01:44:20.044 --> 01:44:21.920
-I'll tell them everything.
-I don't want you to do that.

1270
01:44:22.005 --> 01:44:23.006
You're not who they say you are.

1271
01:44:23.089 --> 01:44:25.132
-Please. please just--
-Listen for a minute. Just promise me!

1272
01:44:26.676 --> 01:44:29.095
Why would you ask me to promise that?

1273
01:44:34.267 --> 01:44:36.143
Because they need someone to be wicked.

1274
01:44:37.729 --> 01:44:39.063
so that you can be good.

1275
01:44:45.528 --> 01:44:47.696
♪ <i>I'm limited</i> ♪

1276
01:44:48.823 --> 01:44:49.949
Just look at me.

1277
01:44:52.827 --> 01:44:55.955
Not with your eyes. with theirs.

1278
01:45:00.251 --> 01:45:03.003
♪ <i>I'm limited</i> ♪

1279
01:45:04.881 --> 01:45:09.381
♪ <i>And just look at you
You can do all I couldn't do</i> ♪

1280
01:45:12.180 --> 01:45:13.806
♪ <i>Glinda</i> ♪

1281
01:45:44.212 --> 01:45:46.589
Here. Take it.

1282
01:45:47.298 --> 01:45:48.632
-What? Elphie--
-Go on.

1283
01:45:48.716 --> 01:45:50.217
Take it.

1284
01:45:50.301 --> 01:45:53.304
But you know I can't read this. I--

1285
01:45:53.388 --> 01:45:54.555
Well. you have to learn.

1286
01:45:56.057 --> 01:45:57.975
We can't let "good" be just a word.

1287
01:45:59.727 --> 01:46:01.145
It has to mean something.

1288
01:46:03.815 --> 01:46:05.566
It has to change things.

1289
01:46:10.822 --> 01:46:15.322
♪ <i>Because now it's up to you</i> ♪

1290
01:46:18.580 --> 01:46:19.622
For both of us.

1291
01:46:24.836 --> 01:46:29.336
♪ <i>Now it's up to you</i> ♪

1292
01:46:43.938 --> 01:46:45.189
You know. um...

1293
01:46:50.862 --> 01:46:52.864
You're the only friend I ever had.

1294
01:46:55.950 --> 01:46:57.451
And I've had so many friends...

1295
01:47:01.581 --> 01:47:03.165
...but only one that mattered.

1296
01:47:05.752 --> 01:47:07.670
♪ <i>I've heard it said</i> ♪

1297
01:47:09.172 --> 01:47:13.672
♪ <i>That people come into our lives
For a reason</i> ♪

1298
01:47:16.054 --> 01:47:19.390
♪ <i>Bringing something we must learn</i> ♪

1299
01:47:19.474 --> 01:47:23.974
♪ <i>And we are led
To those who help us most to grow</i> ♪

1300
01:47:26.940 --> 01:47:28.358
♪ <i>If we let them</i> ♪

1301
01:47:30.068 --> 01:47:32.904
♪ <i>And we help them in return</i> ♪

1302
01:47:34.238 --> 01:47:38.738
♪ <i>Well. I don't know
If I believe that's true</i> ♪

1303
01:47:40.119 --> 01:47:43.455
♪ <i>But I know I am who I am today</i> ♪

1304
01:47:43.539 --> 01:47:46.917
♪ <i>Because I knew you</i> ♪

1305
01:47:48.544 --> 01:47:53.044
♪ <i>Like a comet pulled from orbit
As it passes a sun</i> ♪

1306
01:47:55.259 --> 01:47:59.759
♪ <i>Like a stream that meets a boulder
Halfway through the wood</i> ♪

1307
01:48:03.309 --> 01:48:07.809
♪ <i>Who can say if I've been changed
For the better?</i> ♪

1308
01:48:09.190 --> 01:48:12.484
♪ <i>But because I knew you</i> ♪

1309
01:48:17.573 --> 01:48:22.073
♪ <i>I have been changed for good</i> ♪

1310
01:48:28.626 --> 01:48:33.126
♪ <i>It well may be
That we will never meet again</i> ♪

1311
01:48:35.550 --> 01:48:38.344
♪ <i>In this lifetime</i> ♪

1312
01:48:38.428 --> 01:48:42.223
<i>So let me say before we part</i>

1313
01:48:42.306 --> 01:48:46.806
♪ <i>So much of me is made
Of what I learned from you</i> ♪

1314
01:48:48.646 --> 01:48:52.107
♪ <i>You'll be with me</i> ♪

1315
01:48:52.191 --> 01:48:56.320
♪ <i>Like a handprint on my heart</i> ♪

1316
01:48:56.404 --> 01:49:00.904
♪ <i>And now whatever way
Our stories end</i> ♪

1317
01:49:02.535 --> 01:49:05.913
♪ <i>I know you have rewritten mine</i> ♪

1318
01:49:05.997 --> 01:49:10.209
♪ <i>By being my friend</i> ♪

1319
01:49:10.293 --> 01:49:14.793
♪ <i>Like a ship blown from its mooring
By a wind off the sea</i> ♪

1320
01:49:17.133 --> 01:49:21.633
♪ <i>Like a seed dropped by a sky bird
In a distant wood</i> ♪

1321
01:49:24.766 --> 01:49:29.266
♪ <i>Who can say if I've been changed
For the better?</i> ♪

1322
01:49:30.563 --> 01:49:33.857
♪ <i>But because I knew you</i> ♪

1323
01:49:34.525 --> 01:49:37.236
♪ <i>Because I knew you</i> ♪

1324
01:49:37.320 --> 01:49:41.820
♪ <i>I have been changed for good</i> ♪

1325
01:49:42.617 --> 01:49:45.161
♪ <i>And just to clear the air</i> ♪

1326
01:49:45.244 --> 01:49:49.744
♪ <i>I ask forgiveness for the things
I've done you blame me for</i> ♪

1327
01:49:53.252 --> 01:49:57.752
♪ <i>But then I guess
We know there's blame to share</i> ♪

1328
01:49:58.424 --> 01:50:02.924
♪ <i>And none of it seems to matter anymore</i> ♪

1329
01:50:05.264 --> 01:50:09.764
-♪ <i>Like a comet pulled from orbit</i> ♪
-♪ <i>Like a ship blown from its mooring</i> ♪

1330
01:50:10.061 --> 01:50:12.313
-♪ <i>As it passes a sun</i> ♪
-♪ <i>By a wind off the sea</i> ♪

1331
01:50:12.396 --> 01:50:14.648
♪ <i>Like a stream that meets a boulder</i> ♪

1332
01:50:14.732 --> 01:50:17.025
♪ <i>Like a seed dropped
By a bird in the wood</i> ♪

1333
01:50:17.110 --> 01:50:19.237
♪ <i>Halfway through the wood</i> ♪

1334
01:50:19.320 --> 01:50:23.820
♪ <i>Who can say if I've been changed</i> ♪

1335
01:50:25.618 --> 01:50:27.661
♪ <i>For the better?</i> ♪

1336
01:50:28.329 --> 01:50:32.829
♪ <i>I do believe I have been changed
For the better</i> ♪

1337
01:50:36.879 --> 01:50:40.966
♪ <i>And because I knew you</i> ♪

1338
01:50:42.760 --> 01:50:46.180
♪ <i>Because I knew you</i> ♪

1339
01:50:48.141 --> 01:50:52.641
♪ <i>Because I knew you</i> ♪

1340
01:50:53.646 --> 01:50:58.146
♪ <i>I have been changed</i> ♪

1341
01:51:06.033 --> 01:51:10.533
♪ <i>For good</i> ♪

1342
01:51:24.010 --> 01:51:25.970
Come on. Come on. Quick.

1343
01:51:27.388 --> 01:51:28.764
No one can know you were here.

1344
01:51:36.397 --> 01:51:38.023
-You stay here.
-What?

1345
01:51:38.107 --> 01:51:39.733
Everything's gonna be fine.

1346
01:51:40.568 --> 01:51:41.569
I love you.

1347
01:51:44.280 --> 01:51:45.406
I love you too.

1348
01:52:41.712 --> 01:52:46.212
♪ <i>And Goodness knows</i> ♪

1349
01:52:47.551 --> 01:52:52.051
♪ <i>The Wicked's lives are lonely</i> ♪

1350
01:52:53.808 --> 01:52:57.061
♪ <i>Goodness knows</i> ♪

1351
01:52:57.144 --> 01:53:01.644
♪ <i>The Wicked die alone</i> ♪

1352
01:54:20.853 --> 01:54:21.854
Oh. Elphie...

1353
01:54:39.038 --> 01:54:41.040
Miss Glinda.

1354
01:55:19.703 --> 01:55:20.704
She's dead.

1355
01:55:23.791 --> 01:55:25.709
-Do you have her broomstick?
-No.

1356
01:55:26.919 --> 01:55:29.212
But I do have something else
that belonged to her.

1357
01:55:29.296 --> 01:55:31.923
It was a keepsake. She told me herself.

1358
01:55:32.007 --> 01:55:33.425
It belonged to her mother.

1359
01:55:35.803 --> 01:55:36.887
This belonged to...

1360
01:55:39.014 --> 01:55:40.140
her mother?

1361
01:56:21.765 --> 01:56:23.767
So Elphaba was yours all along.

1362
01:56:23.851 --> 01:56:28.351
That's why she had such powers.
she was a child of both worlds.

1363
01:56:29.064 --> 01:56:31.733
Oh. my Lord.

1364
01:56:33.402 --> 01:56:34.486
What have I done?

1365
01:56:37.323 --> 01:56:39.867
You have caused great harm.

1366
01:56:40.618 --> 01:56:42.494
Which is why you will be leaving Oz.

1367
01:56:43.245 --> 01:56:44.246
Today.

1368
01:56:50.419 --> 01:56:52.337
Did you hear what I said?

1369
01:56:53.172 --> 01:56:56.341
And what... what will I tell people?

1370
01:56:57.009 --> 01:56:58.135
Make something up.

1371
01:56:59.803 --> 01:57:01.137
You're good at that.

1372
01:57:24.286 --> 01:57:25.412
Excuse me.

1373
01:57:26.121 --> 01:57:27.163
Hello.

1374
01:57:27.790 --> 01:57:29.875
What? What do you want?

1375
01:57:30.459 --> 01:57:31.668
Look out your window.

1376
01:57:34.046 --> 01:57:36.631
Come on. You don't wanna miss this.

1377
01:57:42.221 --> 01:57:43.972
Excuse me. please.

1378
01:57:44.056 --> 01:57:45.098
Don't leave without us.

1379
01:57:45.182 --> 01:57:47.434
Please. I wanna go home.

1380
01:57:47.518 --> 01:57:49.603
I swear. it never ends with that girl.

1381
01:57:52.940 --> 01:57:56.151
The Wizard is taking
a permanent leave of absence.

1382
01:58:00.281 --> 01:58:03.242
Not a rumor. a fact.

1383
01:58:03.742 --> 01:58:05.452
The kind that is true.

1384
01:58:06.495 --> 01:58:08.413
Glinda. dear.

1385
01:58:08.914 --> 01:58:12.250
Can you not find it in your heart
t-to forgive me?

1386
01:58:13.586 --> 01:58:15.629
As Oz is my witness.

1387
01:58:16.130 --> 01:58:19.133
I can see now how truly good you are.

1388
01:58:21.468 --> 01:58:24.512
Actually. I'm not. Not yet.

1389
01:58:26.015 --> 01:58:27.474
But just think. Madame.

1390
01:58:27.558 --> 01:58:30.852
We have so many cages.
and all recently vacated.

1391
01:58:30.936 --> 01:58:32.437
You'll have your pick.

1392
01:58:32.521 --> 01:58:35.273
Although I can't imagine
you'll hold up very well.

1393
01:58:35.941 --> 01:58:40.441
I mean. my personal opinion is
you do not have what it takes.

1394
01:58:42.156 --> 01:58:43.991
I hope you prove me wrong.

1395
01:58:45.367 --> 01:58:46.493
I doubt you will.

1396
01:58:48.203 --> 01:58:50.997
What are you doing? Let go of me. Let--

1397
01:59:38.587 --> 01:59:42.799
♪ <i>Good news</i> ♪

1398
01:59:43.384 --> 01:59:46.136
♪ <i>She's dead</i> ♪

1399
01:59:46.220 --> 01:59:48.430
♪ <i>The Witch of the West is dead</i> ♪

1400
01:59:48.514 --> 01:59:50.891
♪ <i>The Wickedest Witch there ever was</i> ♪

1401
01:59:50.974 --> 01:59:52.892
♪ <i>The enemy of all of us here in Oz</i> ♪

1402
01:59:52.976 --> 01:59:57.313
♪ <i>Is dead</i> ♪

1403
01:59:57.398 --> 02:00:01.777
♪ <i>Good news</i> ♪

1404
02:00:01.860 --> 02:00:05.530
♪ <i>Good news</i> ♪

1405
02:00:11.120 --> 02:00:13.288
Whoo! Yep.

1406
02:00:14.707 --> 02:00:16.709
Well. this has been fun.

1407
02:00:16.792 --> 02:00:17.793
As you can imagine.

1408
02:00:17.876 --> 02:00:20.503
I have much to attend to
with the Wizard's unexpected departure.

1409
02:00:20.587 --> 02:00:24.882
So if there are no further questions.
I'm gonna go.

1410
02:00:24.967 --> 02:00:25.968
Glinda.

1411
02:00:26.802 --> 02:00:28.887
Is it true you were her friend?

1412
02:00:28.971 --> 02:00:30.389
What?

1413
02:00:30.472 --> 02:00:31.764
Sorry. one sec.

1414
02:00:33.767 --> 02:00:34.726
What?

1415
02:00:35.310 --> 02:00:37.603
Is it true you were her friend?

1416
02:00:41.483 --> 02:00:42.484
Friend?

1417
02:00:44.945 --> 02:00:45.946
Yes.

1418
02:00:47.906 --> 02:00:49.532
I-I mean. I did know her.

1419
02:00:51.869 --> 02:00:52.828
That is.

1420
02:00:54.121 --> 02:00:55.664
our paths did cross.

1421
02:01:01.378 --> 02:01:02.462
At school.

1422
02:01:10.763 --> 02:01:11.764
Wait.

1423
02:01:15.434 --> 02:01:16.893
I have something more to say.

1424
02:01:26.487 --> 02:01:27.738
Fellow Ozians.

1425
02:01:52.429 --> 02:01:54.055
All Ozians.

1426
02:01:55.307 --> 02:01:56.141
Yes. come out.

1427
02:01:56.934 --> 02:01:58.435
Wherever you are. come out.

1428
02:02:03.065 --> 02:02:04.149
Friends.

1429
02:02:07.528 --> 02:02:09.863
Because I don't see any enemies here.

1430
02:02:16.495 --> 02:02:18.330
We have been through a frightening time.

1431
02:02:19.790 --> 02:02:23.418
And there will be other times
and other things that frighten us.

1432
02:02:25.754 --> 02:02:27.046
But if you'll let me...

1433
02:02:29.383 --> 02:02:30.675
I'd like to try to help.

1434
02:02:32.928 --> 02:02:34.220
To change things.

1435
02:02:39.017 --> 02:02:40.601
I'd like to try to be...

1436
02:02:41.228 --> 02:02:42.812
Glinda the Good.

1437
02:03:51.423 --> 02:03:52.424
It worked.

1438
02:03:53.634 --> 02:03:54.968
They all think you're dead.

1439
02:03:55.052 --> 02:03:56.053
Fiyero?

1440
02:04:02.559 --> 02:04:03.560
See?

1441
02:04:06.271 --> 02:04:07.272
Good as new.

1442
02:04:18.784 --> 02:04:20.494
You saved my life.

1443
02:04:30.462 --> 02:04:32.464
You're beautiful.

1444
02:04:35.300 --> 02:04:36.509
You don't have to lie to me.

1445
02:04:38.136 --> 02:04:39.637
It's not lying.

1446
02:04:41.515 --> 02:04:43.016
It's...

1447
02:04:44.267 --> 02:04:46.769
It's looking at things in another way.

1448
02:04:47.938 --> 02:04:49.356
Time to go.

1449
02:05:32.649 --> 02:05:34.859
<i>I wish that
Glinda could know we're alive.</i>

1450
02:05:39.823 --> 02:05:41.157
<i>But I know she can't.</i>

1451
02:05:44.286 --> 02:05:46.079
<i>No one can ever know.</i>

1452
02:06:52.604 --> 02:06:56.691
♪ <i>Who can say</i> ♪

1453
02:06:57.317 --> 02:07:01.817
♪ <i>If I've been changed for the better?</i> ♪

1454
02:07:02.989 --> 02:07:07.489
-♪ <i>But because I knew you</i> ♪
-♪ <i>Because I knew you</i> ♪

1455
02:07:08.411 --> 02:07:12.498
♪ <i>No one mourns the Wicked</i> ♪

1456
02:07:13.667 --> 02:07:18.167
♪ <i>Because I knew you</i> ♪

1457
02:07:20.924 --> 02:07:25.424
♪ <i>I have been changed</i> ♪

1458
02:07:27.097 --> 02:07:31.518
♪ <i>No one mourns the Wicked</i> ♪

1459
02:07:33.770 --> 02:07:36.773
♪ <i>Wicked</i> ♪

1460
02:07:39.568 --> 02:07:44.068
♪ <i>Wicked</i> ♪

1461
02:07:54.624 --> 02:07:59.124
♪ <i>Wicked</i> ♪
